{"_id":"0Dx07D8GhmeMcoDt","name":"Airloo","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:airloo","level":3,"monsterType":"Mythical Beast","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five senses","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Forests, Mountains, Lakeside","reputation":8,"weakness":13,"weakPoint":"Fire damage +3 points","initiative":11,"movementSpeed":"15 (4 Legs) / 15 (On the Water)","fortitude":"5 (12)","willpower":"5 (12)","source":"BM","description":"The Airloo is a mythical beast that is more than 3 meters long and has the appearance of a gigantic goat. It has two large, twisted horns on its head, and its hooves are charged with magic power, allowing it to walk on the surface of the water.\n\nAirloos often live in flocks around lakes deep in mountains and forests and are known to attack anything that comes near them. For this reason, they are called lakeside guardians, and it is believed that someone may have ordered them to protect the lakes in prehistoric times.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Horns (Head)","accuracy":"5 (12)","damage":"2d+1","evasion":"5 (12)","defense":2,"hp":{"value":26,"max":26},"mp":{"value":18,"max":18}},{"style":"Hooves (Body)","accuracy":"4 (11)","damage":"2d+2","evasion":"4 (11)","defense":3,"hp":{"value":30,"max":30},"mp":{"value":11,"max":11}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"Head","description":""},{"title":"► Loud Roar","description":"The Airloo can let loose a loud bellowing roar.\nRoll 2d, and if the roll is 10 or more, a new Airloo appears on the battlefield. The position of the new Airloo is the rearguard area of the Airloo's faction in Simplified Combat, or 15m away in any direction determined by the GM from the position where this ability was used in Standard/Advanced Combat. The new Airloo will begin to act to protect its comrades after 10 seconds (1 round).\nThe GM may adjust the number of Airloo appearing from this unique skill (even to 0, if appropriate), according to the situation.\nThis unique skill cannot be used on consecutive turns."},{"title":"⏩ Stratagem &amp; Maneuver / 1 Area (5m Radius)","description":"Can use [ Surging Offense I ] (Physical Damage +1).\nEvery third turn uses [ Maneuver: Unexpected Blow I ] (Accuracy +2, Damage +2). If there are no characters eligible to be effected by a Stratagem, these abilities will not be used."},{"title":"🗨 Power Strike I","description":"They can deal an additional 4 damage on their next attack. However, any Evasion Check made by them this turn receives a -2 penalty."},{"title":"Body","description":""},{"title":"🗨 Taunting Strike I","description":"A Body can make an attack with reduced damage by -2.\nIf the attack hits, the opponent must attack (with any type of attack) the Body as much as possible within the next 10 seconds (1 round). This does not work for characters with an Intellect score of 18 or higher or on monsters with &quot;Intelligence: High&quot;."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"2 - 7","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"8 - 11","loot":"Fur (150G/Red A)"},{"roll":"12+","loot":"Big Horn (1,000G/Red S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Airloo","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"0Sy4nLn22IclTpiF","name":"Ringing Rain Deer","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:ringing-rain-deer","level":8,"monsterType":"Mythical Beast","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Five senses","disposition":"Neutral","soulscars":0,"languages":"Sylvan","habitat":"Forest","reputation":15,"weakness":18,"weakPoint":"Physical damage +2 points","initiative":16,"movementSpeed":"20 (4 Legs)","fortitude":"10 (17)","willpower":"11 (18)","source":"CR II p. 392","description":"This is a mythical beast looking like a reindeer, with many nut-like bells with altered horns attached to various parts of the big horns. By shaking its head, the bells on the horns ring, creating spellsongs.\n\nCautious, they seldom appear in front of anyone except those they trust. When an intruder comes to their territory, they try to drive them away with spellsongs.\n\nWhen acquired as loot, their bells may be used as materials for musical instruments, sacred treasures, ritual implements, etc.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Hoof","accuracy":"11 (18)","damage":"2d+11","evasion":"10 (17)","defense":7,"hp":{"value":68,"max":68},"mp":{"value":27,"max":27}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"► Basic Spellsongs 5 Level/9 (16)/All areas (50m Radius)","description":""},{"title":"► Special Spellsong /9 (16)/All areas (50m Radius)","description":"Uses the Spellsongs [ Nostalgia ] and [ Lullaby ]. Once this unique skill is used, it cannot be used for the next 30 seconds (3 rounds). After using either Spellsong, 30 seconds (3 rounds) must elapse before the subsequent use of either special Spellsong."},{"title":"► [ Finale: Breath of the Meadows ]/9 (16)","description":"Within &quot;Range: 2 (60m),&quot; up to 3 characters heal their HP by 2d+7 points. This effect does not work on Undead, Constructs, and Magitech characters.\nThis unique skill cannot be used in consecutive turns. Also, once a character has been affected, it cannot be affected for the following hour."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Light Sounding Bell (200G/Gold Red Black A) x 1d"},{"roll":"2 - 10","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"11+","loot":"Clear Sounding Bell (2,680G/Gold Red Black S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Ringing Rain Deer","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"0uB3yz5v4iyDyXDb","name":"Hellhound","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:hellhound","level":4,"monsterType":"Mythical Beast","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Ruins","reputation":9,"weakness":15,"weakPoint":"Water/Ice damage + 3 points","initiative":16,"movementSpeed":"18 (4 Legs)","fortitude":"6 (13)","willpower":"7 (14)","source":"CR I p. 426","description":"Hellhounds are large dogs with jet-black fur, often seen spitting gouts of flame. It is sometimes found in and around a Shallow Abyss, which is why it is also called &quot;Watchdogs of Hell&quot;.\n\nRarely, a red stone with a faint heat may be found inside its body.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Bite","accuracy":"7 (14)","damage":"2d+4","evasion":"6 (13)","defense":2,"hp":{"value":38,"max":38},"mp":{"value":20,"max":20}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Fire Immunity","description":""},{"title":"► Fire Breath/5 (12)/Fortitude/Half","description":"A Hellhound breathes fire in a &quot;Range: Touch&quot;, dealing 2d + 4 Fire magic damage to up to 3 targets.\nThis unique skill cannot be used in consecutive rounds."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"2 - 3","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"4 - 11","loot":"Mythical Beast Hide (140G/Red A)"},{"roll":"12+","loot":"Flame Crystal (1,600G/Gold S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Hellhound","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"1Q9qwJ3oFH0lwuUA","name":"Python","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:python","level":9,"monsterType":"Mythical Beast","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Swamp, Marsh","reputation":15,"weakness":19,"weakPoint":"Physical damage +2 points","initiative":17,"movementSpeed":"20(Crawling)","fortitude":"12 (19)","willpower":"12 (19)","source":"CR III p. 395","description":"It is a poison snake, always spreading poison and noxious gases. Its total length is about 10 meters, but its thick body, covered with black and purple scales, makes it quite a presence.\n\nThey intensely hate Humanoid, Barbarous, and all other creatures with intelligence, and once they encounter one, they will never relent in their attacks until they have completely defeated it.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Bite (Head)","accuracy":"12 (19)","damage":"2d+12","evasion":"11 (18)","defense":9,"hp":{"value":79,"max":79},"mp":{"value":19,"max":19}},{"style":"Slam (Body)","accuracy":"11 (18)","damage":"2d+10","evasion":"10 (17)","defense":11,"hp":{"value":88,"max":88},"mp":{"value":19,"max":19}},{"style":"Tail (Tail)","accuracy":"12 (19)","damage":"2d+14","evasion":"10 (17)","defense":9,"hp":{"value":72,"max":72},"mp":{"value":12,"max":12}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"All Sections","description":""},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity","description":""},{"title":"Head","description":""},{"title":"◯ Poison/12 (19)/Fortitude/Negates","description":"If the Bite hits, it deals 8 poison magic damage to the target."},{"title":"► Poison Spray/11 (18)/Fortitude/Half","description":"Within &quot;Range/Area: 2 (30m) / Shot &quot; spits poison on &quot;Target: 1 Character&quot;, dealing 2d+9 Poison magic damage.\nThis ability cannot be used on consecutive turns."},{"title":"Body","description":""},{"title":"◯ Poisonous Fog/11 (18)/Fortitude/Half","description":"A poisonous mist is constantly emitted from the body.\nAt the end of this monster's turn, all the characters in the same position (area, coordinate) as the Body section suffer 2d+6 Poison magic damage."},{"title":"Tail","description":""},{"title":"🗨 Tail Sweep","description":"The monster can use its tail to attack up to 5 targets in the same skirmish. An Accuracy check is made on all characters at once, and damage is determined individually.\nThis attack cannot be used in consecutive rounds."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"2 - 11","loot":"Venom of the Woe Serpent (1,000G/Red S)"},{"roll":"12+","loot":"Large Amount of Venom (10,000G/Red SS)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Python","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"3Ik1tGeDylZXyRuu","name":"Cherub","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:cherub","level":5,"monsterType":"Mythical Beast","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five senses","disposition":"Neutral","soulscars":0,"languages":"Arcana","habitat":"Mountains","reputation":12,"weakness":15,"weakPoint":"Energy type damage +3 points","initiative":11,"movementSpeed":"20 (4 Legs) / 20 (Flying)","fortitude":"6 (13)","willpower":"7 (14)","source":"BM","description":"A Cherub is a mythical beast in the shape of a winged dog about 1 meter long. In some regions, it is believed to be a messenger of the gods, and it is said that those who see it will be blessed with good fortune.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Bite","accuracy":"7 (14)","damage":"2d+8","evasion":"7 (14)","defense":5,"hp":{"value":38,"max":38},"mp":{"value":46,"max":46}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"► Spiritualism Magic , Divine Magic 5 Level / Magic Power 8 (15)","description":""},{"title":"◯ 🗨 ► Magic Aptitude","description":"They can use the Combat Feats [ Targeting ], [ Metamagic/Time ], and [ Wordbreak ]."},{"title":"⏩ Sacred Beast Blessing","description":"Cherub pats &quot;Target: 1 Character&quot; within &quot;Range: Touch&quot; with its feathers and gives a blessing. The target recovers 3 MP at the end of its turn for 1 minute (6 rounds).\nThis unique skill can be used only once per round."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"2 - 5","loot":"Mythical Beast Hide (140G/Red A)"},{"roll":"6 - 9","loot":"Fine Mythical Beast Hide (300G/Red A)"},{"roll":"10+","loot":"Beautiful Mythical Beast Hide (800G/Gold Red A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Cherub","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"8znnlnaYuG43lJxU","name":"Cocollona","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:cocollona","level":12,"monsterType":"Mythical Beast","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Neutral","soulscars":0,"languages":"Trade Common, Sylvan, Daemonic","habitat":"Human villages, Shallows","reputation":16,"weakness":22,"weakPoint":"Accuracy +1","initiative":18,"movementSpeed":"14 (4 Legs) / 25 (Flying)","fortitude":"15(22)","willpower":"16(23)","source":"AB, p. 119","description":"This Mythical Beast has a wingspan of several meters and possesses the wings of a giant butterfly on a crocodilian body. Despite its fearsome appearance, it generally has a gentle temperament and tends to protect those who face unjust treatment, which has led to it being revered as a guardian deity in some regions. However, it shows absolutely no mercy to those who threaten its protected targets, attacking them with magic, the dispersal of scales that cause hallucinations, and an aerial death roll where it bites with powerful jaws and spins in mid-air. While it primarily uses Fairy Magic, specimens that appear in the Shallow Abysses also use Abyssal Magic.\n\nThe Cocollona can make its entire body semi-transparent. However, it cannot use this ability under moonlight, so it is said that if one must fight a Cocollona, they should do so at night.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Bite (Jaw)","accuracy":"15(22)","damage":"2d+16","evasion":"&#32;","defense":14,"hp":{"value":10,"max":10},"mp":{"value":32,"max":32}},{"style":"None (Head)","accuracy":"-","damage":"-","evasion":"&#32;","defense":14,"hp":{"value":9,"max":9},"mp":{"value":32,"max":32}},{"style":"Tail (Body)","accuracy":"16(23)","damage":"2d+16","evasion":"&#32;","defense":13,"hp":{"value":9,"max":9},"mp":{"value":32,"max":32}},{"style":"Wings (Wings)","accuracy":"15(22)","damage":"2d+12","evasion":"&#32;","defense":14,"hp":{"value":6,"max":6},"mp":{"value":32,"max":32}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"All Sections","description":""},{"title":"◯Appears in Moonlight","description":"The entire body is semi-transparent.\nThis monster does not create shielding even when on the battlefield. Additionally, characters in different areas (Simplified Combat) or at coordinates more than 10m away (Advanced/Expert Combat) cannot perceive this monster.\nUnder moonlight, this effect is lost."},{"title":"Jaw &amp; Body","description":""},{"title":"◯Attack Obstacle = Impossible • +4","description":"Its size hinders attacks.\nThe Head section cannot be targeted by melee attacks and gains a +4 bonus to Evasion checks against ranged attacks.\nIf either Jaw or Body section's HP falls to 0 or below, this ability changes to [Attack Obstacle = +4 • None] (only +4 bonus to Evasion checks against melee attacks),&quot; and if both HP reach 0, the ability is completely lost."},{"title":"Jaw","description":""},{"title":"◯Catch and Hold","description":"When a Bite attack hits, it grabs and holds the target. The target becomes immobilized, and from the next round onwards, bite attacks and [►Death Roll] automatically hit.\nWhen the target attempts to escape, it follows the de-bonding rules (see CR III, p. 327, ML, p. 71). This monster itself can automatically release the held target as a Minor Action.\nWhile holding a character with this ability, the Jaw section cannot attack other characters."},{"title":"►Death Roll / Can't","description":"This effect can only target a character being held by [◯Catch and Hold]. Additionally, it cannot be used if either Body or Wings section's HP is 0 or below.\nWhile maintaining its Bite, it violently rotates its body to tear apart the target. Deals 2d+32 points of physical damage to the target. Using this effect does not end the [◯Catch and Hold]."},{"title":"Head","description":""},{"title":"► Fairy Magic 9 Level / Magic Power 11 (18)","description":"The types used are &quot;Water/Ice&quot;, &quot;Wind&quot;, &quot;Light&quot; and &quot;Dark.&quot; If you use contract rules (see MA, p. 136), you can choose from the three types (12 ranks) of &quot;Water/Ice&quot;, &quot;Light&quot; and &quot;Dark.&quot;"},{"title":"◯🗨►Magic Aptitude","description":"They can use Combat Feats [ Targeting ], [ Magic Convergence ], [ Magic Control ], [ Hawk Eye ], [ Universal Metamagic ], [ Violentcast I ], and [ Wordbreak ]."},{"title":"► Abyssal Magic 9 Level /Magic Power 11 (18) (Shallow)","description":"Abyssal Magic can only be used within a Shallow Abyss.\nEnhancement effects can be used up to 3 rounds."},{"title":"◯Limited 2 Actions (Shallow)","description":"The Head section can perform two Major Actions per round in a Shallow Abyss.\nHowever, the Head section cannot use the same type of magic twice (it is possible to use Fairy Magic and Abyssal Magic once each, and there is no limit to the use of Minor Actions)."},{"title":"Body","description":""},{"title":"🗨Tail Sweep","description":"Chooses up to 5 characters capable of melee attacks and performs a Tail attack against them.\nThis ability cannot be used in consecutive turns."},{"title":"Wings","description":""},{"title":"◯Flight","description":"All sections gain a +1 bonus to Accuracy and Evasion checks for melee attacks. This ability is lost if Wings section's HP falls below to 0 or less."},{"title":"►Illusory Scales / 14 (21) / Willpower / Negates","description":"Scatters scales with illusory effects in &quot;Range: Caster&quot; targeting &quot;1 Area (5m radius) / All.&quot;\nTargets who fail their resistance check will see their opponents as fragile maidens (or whatever being they feel most protective of) when attempting weapon attacks, causing their attacks to weaken. They receive a -2 penalty to Accuracy checks, and the damage dealt by their attacks is reduced by 4.\nCountermeasures and remedies effective against either Poison type or Psychic type work against this effect.\nThis ability cannot be used in consecutive turns."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Dazzling Scales (600G/Gold Red A) x 2d"},{"roll":"2 - 5","loot":"Superior Crocodile Skin (600G/Red A)"},{"roll":"6 - 8","loot":"Perfect Crocodile Skin (1,200G/Red S)"},{"roll":"9+","loot":"Supreme Crocodile Skin (2,200G/Red S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Cocollona","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"9JGreurd5Xb2AO6G","name":"Antar","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:antar","level":7,"monsterType":"Mythical Beast","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five senses","disposition":"Neutral","soulscars":0,"languages":"Trade Common, Arcana","habitat":"Forests, Mountains","reputation":15,"weakness":18,"weakPoint":"Magic damage +2 points","initiative":13,"movementSpeed":"15 (4 Legs)","fortitude":"10 (17)","willpower":"10 (17)","source":"Monstrous Lore p. 177","description":"This is a mythical beast that looks like an antelope. Its mouth resembles a human-like shape, and it can speak Humanoid languages.\n\nIts goal is to protect the deep and quiet environment of the forest. When an invasion occurs in their territory, they will try to guide invaders out of the forest and, if impossible, eliminate them.\n\nIn some cases, they have been seen spending time with Humanoids and others who have chosen to live in symbiosis with the forest.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Horns","accuracy":"8 (15)","damage":"2d+8","evasion":"9 (16)","defense":6,"hp":{"value":52,"max":52},"mp":{"value":68,"max":68}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"► Nature Magic 7 Level/Magic Power 10 (17)","description":""},{"title":"◯ 🗨 Magic Aptitude","description":"They can use the Combat Feats [ Targeting ], [ Magic Convergence ], [ Magic Control ]."},{"title":"⏩ Wrath of the Forest","description":"It expresses anger at those who disturb the forest.\nFor 3 minutes (18 rounds), its Accuracy and Spellcasting checks get a +1 bonus.\nThis ability can be used only when its HP is less than half. After using this ability, Antar cannot cancel the effect by itself and will not stop fighting until it eliminates the enemy."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"2 - 6","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"7 - 10","loot":"Grayish-White Fur (600G/Red A)"},{"roll":"11+","loot":"Silvery-White Fur (2,100G/Gold Red S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Antar","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"9pJaIk0ztEDXNFbp","name":"Sphinx","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:sphinx","level":15,"monsterType":"Mythical Beast","intelligence":"High","perception":"Five senses","disposition":"Neutral","soulscars":0,"languages":"All","habitat":"Ruins","reputation":18,"weakness":25,"weakPoint":"Physical damage +2 points","initiative":20,"movementSpeed":"20 (4 Legs)/40 (Flying)","fortitude":"20 (27)","willpower":"22 (29)","source":"CR III p. 398","description":"The Sphinx is a mythical beast about 5m tall, with the body of a lion, the wings of an eagle, and the face of a beautiful human woman. Highly intelligent and powerful wizards in their own right, Sphinxes can speak any language and cast the most known magic spells, regardless of Class. Sphinxes are often seen serving as gatekeepers for ancient magicians, welcoming those who can answer their riddles as friends of the magician. However, failing to come up with the correct response will lead to a dire fate.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Bite (Head)","accuracy":"20 (27)","damage":"2d+16","evasion":"17 (24)","defense":15,"hp":{"value":137,"max":137},"mp":{"value":194,"max":194}},{"style":"Claws (Body)","accuracy":"21 (28)","damage":"2d+13","evasion":"16 (23)","defense":16,"hp":{"value":147,"max":147},"mp":{"value":84,"max":84}},{"style":"Wing (Wing)","accuracy":"19 (26)","damage":"2d+10","evasion":"18 (25)","defense":13,"hp":{"value":81,"max":81},"mp":{"value":84,"max":84}},{"style":"Wing (Wing)","accuracy":"19 (26)","damage":"2d+10","evasion":"18 (25)","defense":13,"hp":{"value":81,"max":81},"mp":{"value":84,"max":84}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"All Sections","description":""},{"title":"◯ Mana Resistance","description":"Reduce all Magic Damage Sphinx receive by -5."},{"title":"◯ Knowledge Incarnate &amp; Weakness Exploit","description":"Sphinx can make Sage Knowledge checks with a standard value of 20. In this case, it knows combat feat [Sage's Wisdom].\nSphinx deals double damage to other monster weak points it detected."},{"title":"Head","description":""},{"title":"► Magic (All Systems) 13 Level/Magic Power 19 (26)","description":"It has mastered all magic systems at 13 levels.\nFor Fairy Magic, it can use all types of magic up to rank 13."},{"title":"◯ Multiple Declarations = 3 times","description":""},{"title":"◯ 🗨 ► Magic Aptitude","description":"The Sphinx can use all Combat Feats that are &quot;Use: Wizard-Type Classes&quot; and [ Multi-Action ], [ Targeting ], [ Hawk Eye ], [ Metamagic Master ], [ Marionette ], [ Mana Save ], [ MP Save/All Wizard-Type Classes ], and [ Wordbreak ]."},{"title":"⏩ Riddle/20 (27)/Adventurer Level + Intelligence Modifier/Negates","description":"The Sphinx can ask &quot;Target: 1 Entire Character&quot; within &quot;Range/Area: 2 (100m) / Target &quot; a riddle. This Riddle cannot be prevented even if the target is unable to hear or speak. On a failed roll, the target cannot move or perform Major Actions or Minor Actions for 30 seconds (3 rounds). This effect is of Curse + Psychic type.\nThis unique skill can be used only once per round."},{"title":"Body","description":""},{"title":"◯ Attack Obstacle = +4 • None","description":"The Sphinx's huge body blocks attacks. Against melee attacks, the Head section receives a +4 bonus to Evasion checks.\nThis effect disappears when the Body section falls to 0 HP or lower."},{"title":"Wing","description":""},{"title":"◯ Flight","description":"All sections receive a +1 bonus to Accuracy and Evasion only for melee attacks.\nIf any of the Wings fall to 0 HP or lower, this unique skill cannot be used."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Feathers (1,000G/Red S)"},{"roll":"2 - 9","loot":"Ancient Runestones (2,000G/White S)"},{"roll":"10 - 12","loot":"Engraved Signet Ring (5,000G/Gold White S)"},{"roll":"13+","loot":"Mysterious Lithograph (10,000G/White SS)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Sphinx","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"AF9or36YycsujZkW","name":"Golden Ash","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:golden-ash","level":14,"monsterType":"Mythical Beast","intelligence":"Animal","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Labyrinths, Ruins","reputation":18,"weakness":22,"weakPoint":"Bludgeoning damage +3 points","initiative":0,"movementSpeed":"30 (Fluid) / -","fortitude":"17 (24)","willpower":"17 (24)","source":"BM","description":"Golden Ash is a swarm of very small insects with golden shells. The entire swarm shares a single consciousness and acts as a single organism.\n\nGolden Ash inhabits ruins and underground labyrinths and usually remains still and calm. In this state, Golden Ash looks like a pile of gold dust, and adventurers dazzled by its treasures may carelessly approach it and become its victims. The Golden Ash devours the bones of its poor victims, and then once again mimics gold dust as it waits for the next victim to come along. When the Golden Ash is defeated, the silver coins and jewelry of its former victims can be found buried among its remains.","combatStyles":[{"style":"None","accuracy":"-","damage":"-","evasion":"16 (23)","defense":14,"hp":{"value":120,"max":120},"mp":{"value":33,"max":33}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Mimicry / 25 / Danger Sense / Negates","description":"It mimics gold sand. While mimicking, characters cannot perform a Monster Knowledge check on this monster. If a character approaches it unintentionally, they need to make a Danger check with Target Number 25, and if it fails, they will be surprised. Mimicry will automatically end once the monster starts to act.\nThis monster can be detected with [ Sense Magic ]."},{"title":"► Devouring Swarm/Can ’ t","description":"Countless swarms of golden dust crawl up and attack the target. It deals 2d + 1/5 of Golden Ash remaining HP (rounded down) magic damage to a character within a Melee Attack range."},{"title":"◯ Wriggling Swarm","description":"It is immune from criticals from any weapon attacks.\nIt cannot be the target of Throw or similar attacks.\nIt can receive only 1 applied magic damage from &quot;Area: Target&quot; and &quot;Target: 1 Character&quot; magic and effects.\nCharacters cannot use Combat Feats [ Targeting ] or [ Magic Control ] in the skirmish areas where this monster resides on any character within, including Golden Ash."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Bag of Silver (100G/-) x 2d"},{"roll":"2 - 6","loot":"Gems (150G/Gold A) x 2d"},{"roll":"7 - 10","loot":"Gems (300G/Gold A) x 2d"},{"roll":"11+","loot":"Gems (500G/Gold A) x 2d"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Golden Ash","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"AVTHzMG26JrGDuK5","name":"Thunderbird","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:thunderbird","level":5,"monsterType":"Mythical Beast","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Five senses","disposition":"Hungry","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Mountains","reputation":10,"weakness":16,"weakPoint":"Magic Damage +2 points","initiative":14,"movementSpeed":"-/50 (Flying)","fortitude":"8 (15)","willpower":"8 (15)","source":"CR I p. 427","description":"A huge bird cloaked in lightning, a Thunderbird's body shines brightly in the sky. Even amid combat, the electricity arcing off of one of these great birds is rather intense.\n\nThunderbirds often do not stay in one territory for long and are difficult to track down for any purpose. Only rarely does a Thunderbird settle down and create a nest, and more often than not it is due to spawning.\n\nThey may lay eggs in Shallow Abysses for self-preservation, which can create dangerous beasts for intruders.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Beak (Body)","accuracy":"7 (14)","damage":"2d+8","evasion":"7 (14)","defense":5,"hp":{"value":37,"max":37},"mp":{"value":22,"max":22}},{"style":"Wing (Wing)","accuracy":"8 (15)","damage":"2d+6","evasion":"6 (13)","defense":3,"hp":{"value":28,"max":28},"mp":{"value":10,"max":10}},{"style":"Wing (Wing)","accuracy":"8 (15)","damage":"2d+6","evasion":"6 (13)","defense":3,"hp":{"value":28,"max":28},"mp":{"value":10,"max":10}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"All Sections","description":""},{"title":"◯ Lightning Immunity","description":""},{"title":"Body","description":""},{"title":"► Thunderclap/6 (13)/Willpower/Half","description":"Summons lightning with &quot;Range: Self&quot; and &quot;Target: 1 area (6m radius) / 20&quot; and deals 2d+4 Lightning magic damage to the target.\nThis ability cannot be used on consecutive turns."},{"title":"Wing","description":""},{"title":"◯ Flight","description":"A Thunderbird receives a +1 bonus to Accuracy and Evasion only for melee attacks.\nIf one of the Wings falls to 0 HP or lower, this unique skill cannot be used."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"2 - 7","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"8 - 10","loot":"Mystical Beak (350G/Red A)"},{"roll":"11+","loot":"Lightning Crystal (1,600G/Gold S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Thunderbird","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"CKJva3uKN7rI7gqx","name":"Lesser Manticore","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:lesser-manticore","level":6,"monsterType":"Mythical Beast","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Neutral","soulscars":0,"languages":"Arcana, Sylvan","habitat":"Labyrinths","reputation":11,"weakness":16,"weakPoint":"Wind damage +3 points","initiative":14,"movementSpeed":"15 (4 Legs)/23 (Flying)","fortitude":"8 (15)","willpower":"9 (16)","source":"BM","description":"This is a Mythical Beast with the body of a lion, bat wings on its back, a scorpion tail, and an old man's face. The Lesser species is approximately 3 meters long.\n\nHighly intelligent, Lesser Manticores possess extensive knowledge of magic and history. They have a deep understanding of the world, sword mythology, and various civilizations. However, they are vile creatures, both mentally and physically twisted, and do not share their knowledge honestly.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Claw (Front)","accuracy":"9 (16)","damage":"2d+7","evasion":"8 (15)","defense":6,"hp":{"value":58,"max":58},"mp":{"value":52,"max":52}},{"style":"Tail (Rear)","accuracy":"8 (15)","damage":"2d+9","evasion":"7 (14)","defense":4,"hp":{"value":52,"max":52},"mp":{"value":18,"max":18}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"Front","description":""},{"title":"► Truespeech Magic , Spiritualism Magic 5 Level / Magic Power 8 (15)","description":"If you have introduced Deep Magic , it can also cast Deep Magic at the same level and Magic Power."},{"title":"► Fairy Magic 3 Level / Magic Power 6 (13)","description":"Can use Earth, Water/Ice, Fire, and Dark types.\nThis does not change even if the contract pattern is adopted (see MA, p. 136)."},{"title":"⏩ △ Techniques","description":"They may use the [ Cat's Eyes ] and [ Beetleskin ] Techniques."},{"title":"Back","description":""},{"title":"◯ Numbing Poison / 8 (15) / Fortitude / Negates","description":"If the Tail's attack hits and deals 1 or more points of applied damage, it will paralyze the target and reduce its Dexterity by -6 points (to a minimum of 0). This effect is cumulative, and when the Dexterity reaches 0, the target will be unable to make any melee or ranged attacks.\nIf the character has a fixed value, its Accuracy check is reduced by -1 for each effect of this poison, and the character cannot be attacked after three such effects.\nThis effect is Poison type and lasts for 1 hour."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"2 - 6","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"7 - 8","loot":"Fine Mythical Beast Hide (300G/Red A)"},{"roll":"10+","loot":"Beautiful Mythical Beast Hide (800G/Gold Red A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Lesser Manticore","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"F5JcoSkzx06aC4yf","name":"Calcolu","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:calcolu","level":3,"monsterType":"Mythical Beast","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Caves, Swamps, Shallows","reputation":11,"weakness":14,"weakPoint":"Fire damage +3","initiative":10,"movementSpeed":"10 (Crawling)","fortitude":"6 (13)","willpower":"4 (11)","source":"AB, p. 115","description":"This is a mythical beast that resembles a large snail with four tentacles and a fanged mouth. Its body is covered in dense fur, which emphasizes its otherworldly nature. The fur is wet with generated slime, causing sword and bite attacks to slip off.\n\nIt is carnivorous and prefers to entangle its prey with its tentacles before devouring them headfirst. It favors humid environments and often seeks out and settles in Shallow Abyss areas with such characteristics. Occasionally, an Abyss Shard can be found inside its shell.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Tentacle","accuracy":"5(12)","damage":"2d+4","evasion":"&#32;","defense":4,"hp":{"value":3,"max":3},"mp":{"value":32,"max":32}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯Slippery Body","description":"Treated as having 3 points higher Defense against edged weapons. It cannot be targeted by Throw or similar attack methods."},{"title":"◯Abyssal Poison Slime","description":"Characters who perform a melee attack against this monster and land a hit immediately take 2 points of poison fixed damage.\nThis effect only occurs within a Shallow Abyss."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Iron (20G/Black B)"},{"roll":"2 - 9","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"10 - 11","loot":"Abyss Shard (200G/-)"},{"roll":"12+","loot":"Abyss Shard (200G/-) x 2"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Calcolu","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"GCOHuaTjsMDhhZSE","name":"Abyss Toad","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:abyss-toad","level":5,"monsterType":"Mythical Beast","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Neutral","soulscars":0,"languages":"Sylvan, Daemonic","habitat":"Shallows","reputation":12,"weakness":16,"weakPoint":"Fire damage +3 points","initiative":13,"movementSpeed":"10 (4 Legs)","fortitude":"7 (14)","willpower":"7 (14)","source":"AB, p. 116","description":"This is a Mythical Beast that takes the form of a giant toad about 1m in height. Its entire body is embedded with Abyss Shards, and it is believed to have evolved from a Crystal Toad - a Mythical Beast toad with crystals embedded in its body - that adapted to Shallow Abysses. Its body is constantly covered in paralyzing poisonous mucus, which it neutralizes for itself using a button-like stone area embedded in its crown (called a Toad Stone).\n\nWhether through the use of the Abyss Shards embedded in its body or not, it possesses the ability to command lower-ranking Daemons, and is often spotted together with them. While the original Crystal Toad is now believed to be extinct with no recent sightings, encounters with the Abyss Toad still occur in the Shallow.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Tongue","accuracy":"7(14)","damage":"2d+6","evasion":"&#32;","defense":6,"hp":{"value":4,"max":4},"mp":{"value":32,"max":32}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯Poison Immunity","description":""},{"title":"►Pull /7(14)/Evasion/Negates","description":"With &quot;Range/Area: 2 (20m) / Shot &quot; and &quot;Target: 1 Character&quot;, it extends its shooting tongue around its target. Deals 2d+6 points of physical damage to the target and moves them to the same position (area, coordinate) as itself.\nIf the target has multiple sections, no position change occurs, and only damage is dealt."},{"title":"◯Paralyzing Poison / 7 (14) / Fortitude / Negates","description":"Any character who makes a melee attack against this monster and lands a hit must immediately make a Fortitude check. On failure, they receive a -2 penalty to Evasion checks for the next 3 minutes (18 rounds).\nThis effect is Poison type and does not stack."},{"title":"►Guardian Daemon (Shallow)","description":"This effect can only be used within the Shallow Abyss. Summons 1 Daemon. The summoned Daemon is determined by the table, and the MP cost required for summoning varies by Daemon. If the required MP cannot be consumed, the Major Action ends wastefully. Additionally, while a Daemon summoned by this effect already exists on the battlefield, this effect cannot be used again.\n1d | Daemon | MP |\n1 | Erbirea | 18 |\n2 | Dikka | 18 |\n3 | Nuzumal | 36 |\n4 | Aetherbeast | 20 |\n5 | Abyss Minions | 35 |\n6 | Sakkara | 29 |\nThe summoned Daemon will not leave its position and will act according to its own judgment to protect Abyss Toad and eliminate their enemies. However, it will not take any actions to restore HP or MP for any section of this monster.\nThis effect lasts for only 3 minutes (18 rounds). After that, the Daemon is released and begins to act entirely according to its own judgment. At this time, the first thing the Daemon will do is swiftly leave this monster's side. Once this state is reached, even if that Daemon still exists, this monster can summon a new Daemon."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Abyss Shard (200G/-)"},{"roll":"2 - 8","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"9+","loot":"Toad Stone (600G/Gold Red A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Abyss Toad","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"GrBALdBT9x226LoX","name":"Brutal Varg","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:brutal-varg","level":8,"monsterType":"Mythical Beast","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Neutral","soulscars":0,"languages":"Vargian","habitat":"Forests, Plains, Hills","reputation":13,"weakness":18,"weakPoint":"Fire damage + 3 points","initiative":18,"movementSpeed":"20 (4 Legs)","fortitude":"12 (19)","willpower":"10 (17)","source":"Monstrous Lore p. 178","description":"It is one of the larger Vargs and more ferocious than the regular Varg. Only a Barbarous with recognized strength will be allowed to ride on its back.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Bite","accuracy":"11 (18)","damage":"2d+12","evasion":"11 (18)","defense":7,"hp":{"value":78,"max":78},"mp":{"value":27,"max":27}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Coordination","description":"A Brutal Varg gains a bonus to their Accuracy equal to the number of other Vargs (of any type) in the same skirmish, up to a maximum of +4."},{"title":"◯ Rage","description":"When another Varg (of any type) in the same skirmish is defeated, the Brutal Varg gains a cumulative +2 bonus to damage for 10 seconds (1 round).\nThe GM decides when a Varg is defeated (incapacitated or dead)."},{"title":"🗨 Power Strike I","description":"A Varg can deal an additional 4 damage on their next attack. However, any Evasion Check made by them this turn receives a -2 penalty."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"2 - 4","loot":"Mythical Beast Hide (140G/Red A)"},{"roll":"5 - 7","loot":"Fine Mythical Beast Hide (300G/Red A)"},{"roll":"8 - 11","loot":"Beautiful Mythical Beast Hide (800G/Gold Red A)"},{"roll":"12+","loot":"Silver-white Mythical Beast Hide (3,600G/Gold Red S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Brutal Varg","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"GsVOU5UnSoVNOnkx","name":"Kujata","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:kujata","level":12,"monsterType":"Mythical Beast","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five senses","disposition":"Neutral","soulscars":0,"languages":"Sylvan","habitat":"Mountains","reputation":18,"weakness":24,"weakPoint":"Wind damage +3 points","initiative":17,"movementSpeed":"20 (4 Legs)","fortitude":"15 (22)","willpower":"16 (23)","source":"CR III p. 397","description":"This is a mythical beast in the form of a huge hairy buffalo that emits blue phosphorescent light. It has two humps on its back, which crystallize over time and are known to yield high-quality garnets and rubies.\n\nLegend has it that they are the embodiment of the will of the mountain itself and that they have the power to control the climate of the mountain where they live, albeit to a limited extent.\n\nIn many mountains, they are revered as mountain saints, and Kujata himself behaves as such. Although strict in nature, Kujata is basically mild- mannered.\n\nBecause of the constant approach of back gem hunters, Kujata's reaction to Humanoids, Barbarous, and some Mythical Beasts tends to be one of wariness and caution.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Horns (Head)","accuracy":"15 (22)","damage":"2d+16","evasion":"15 (22)","defense":12,"hp":{"value":101,"max":101},"mp":{"value":103,"max":103}},{"style":"Hooves (Front)","accuracy":"16 (23)","damage":"2d+15","evasion":"14 (21)","defense":11,"hp":{"value":109,"max":109},"mp":{"value":44,"max":44}},{"style":"Hooves (Back)","accuracy":"15 (22)","damage":"2d+15","evasion":"14 (21)","defense":11,"hp":{"value":119,"max":119},"mp":{"value":44,"max":44}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"Head","description":""},{"title":"► Fairy Magic 12 Level/Magic Power 15 (22)","description":"Can use Earth, Water/Ice, Wind, and Light types."},{"title":"◯ 🗨 ► Magic Aptitude","description":"They can use the Combat Feats [ Targeting ], [ Magic Convergence ], [ Magic Control ], [ Hawk Eye ], [ Universal Metamagic ], [ Rune Master ], and [ Wordbreak ]."},{"title":"► Limited Weather Control","description":"Kujata can change the weather and temperature in a 10 km radius centered on itself. The weather can be selected from clear skies to heavy rain/heavy snow with 100 mm of rainfall per hour, cloud cover, and rainfall (snowfall). Fog and haze can also be added. This effect works only in mountainous areas and is also limited to the weather-temperatures that can occur in that location and season."},{"title":"Front &amp; Back","description":""},{"title":"◯ Attack Obstacle = Impossible • +4","description":"Kujata's great size hinders attack.\nThe Head cannot be attacked in melee. Against any ranged attacks, Head receives a +4 bonus to Evasion checks.\nIf the HP of either the Front or Back falls to 0 or lower, this unique skill changes to [ ◯ Attack Obstacle = +4 • None (only +4 bonus to Head's Evasion against melee attack)]. If both HPs fall to 0 or lower, the unique skill is completely lost."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Gems (150G/Gold A) x 2d"},{"roll":"Always","loot":"Gems (300G/Gold A) x 1d"},{"roll":"2 - 6","loot":"Gems (500G/Gold A)"},{"roll":"7 - 10","loot":"Rare Gems (1,500G/Gold S)"},{"roll":"11+","loot":"Large Gem (4,000G/Gold S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Kujata","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"HPdeVJJZ5HgYAjTx","name":"Draconet","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:draconet","level":10,"monsterType":"Mythical Beast","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Neutral","soulscars":0,"languages":"Dragonic","habitat":"Various","reputation":15,"weakness":20,"weakPoint":"Physical damage +2 points","initiative":17,"movementSpeed":"13/25(Flying)","fortitude":"13 (20)","willpower":"12 (19)","source":"CR III p. 396","description":"&quot;Draconet&quot; is a name used for dragons 100 years or younger, and a Draconet's attitude reflects its immaturity. Often angry, they will destroy their environment until they either run out of energy or have leveled their surroundings. However, it is possible to communicate with a Draconet when they are in a good mood.\n\nAs with older dragons, Draconets tend to hoard things with a significant amount of stored mana, including magical items, Sword Shards, and even whole Swords of Protection. They loathe to give up any of their hoards but may be convinced if there are appropriate replacements for the items to be taken. While the most common Draconets breathe fire, there are subspecies that can also exhale ice, lightning, or poison.\n\nFor the mount version of this creature, see Draconet (mount) .","combatStyles":[{"style":"Bite (Body)","accuracy":"13 (20)","damage":"2d+14","evasion":"12 (19)","defense":12,"hp":{"value":105,"max":105},"mp":{"value":32,"max":32}},{"style":"Wing (Wing)","accuracy":"12 (19)","damage":"2d+9","evasion":"10 (17)","defense":10,"hp":{"value":66,"max":66},"mp":{"value":16,"max":16}},{"style":"Wing (Wing)","accuracy":"12 (19)","damage":"2d+9","evasion":"10 (17)","defense":10,"hp":{"value":66,"max":66},"mp":{"value":16,"max":16}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"All Sections","description":""},{"title":"◯ Fire Immunity","description":""},{"title":"Body","description":""},{"title":"► Flame Breath/11 (18)/Fortitude/Half","description":"Spits fire at &quot;Target: 1 area(3m Radius) / 5&quot; within &quot;Range/Area: 2 (20m) / Shot &quot; and deals 2d+15 Fire magic damage.\nThis unique skill cannot be used on consecutive turns."},{"title":"Wing","description":""},{"title":"🗨 All-Out Attack","description":"A Wing can deal an additional 8 damage on its next attack. However, any Evasion check made by this section this turn receives a -3 penalty."},{"title":"◯ Flight II","description":"A Draconet receives a +2 bonus to Accuracy and Evasion only for melee attacks.\nIf one of the Wings falls to 0 HP or lower, this unique skill cannot be used."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Dragon Scale (5,000G/Red S)"},{"roll":"2 - 6","loot":"Dragon Fang (1,200G/Red S)"},{"roll":"7+","loot":"Dragon Fang (1,200G/Red S) x 2"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Draconet","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"Hwr5TMN80fhsbqDg","name":"Lesser Dragon","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:lesser-dragon","level":13,"monsterType":"Mythical Beast","intelligence":"High","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Neutral","soulscars":0,"languages":"Trade Common, Draconic, Arcana","habitat":"Cave","reputation":12,"weakness":20,"weakPoint":"Physical damage +2 points","initiative":18,"movementSpeed":"15/30 (Flying)","fortitude":"17 (24)","willpower":"17 (24)","source":"CR II p. 396","description":"A young dragon, less than 500 years of age, yet older than a Draconet . Even though it is relatively young for a Dragon, Lesser Dragons tend to be around 10m long, so any sort of melee attack on the head is nigh impossible.\n\nAble to spit flames and cast spells while flying over the skirmish, a Lesser Dragon's offensive power is second to none. Because of this, Lesser Dragons tend to be very self-centered and overconfident, looking down on others they consider &quot;lesser creatures.&quot; Lesser Dragons look to hoard treasure and valuables, just like any other dragon.\n\nAny brave adventurer (or adventuring party) that can kill a Lesser Dragon will not only earn the title &quot;Dragon Slayer&quot; but will have access to the vast hoard that the dragon had acquired. Additionally, very rarely do dragons have Dragon Eggs inside their bodies, which are incredibly valued on their own due to their use in several magical experiments.\n\nFor the mount version of this creature, see Lesser Dragon (mount) .","combatStyles":[{"style":"Bite (Head)","accuracy":"17 (24)","damage":"2d+18","evasion":"15 (22)","defense":14,"hp":{"value":119,"max":119},"mp":{"value":84,"max":84}},{"style":"Tail (Body)","accuracy":"16 (23)","damage":"2d+16","evasion":"13 (20)","defense":16,"hp":{"value":133,"max":133},"mp":{"value":30,"max":30}},{"style":"Wing (Wing)","accuracy":"15 (22)","damage":"2d+14","evasion":"13 (20)","defense":13,"hp":{"value":84,"max":84},"mp":{"value":28,"max":28}},{"style":"Wing (Wing)","accuracy":"15 (22)","damage":"2d+14","evasion":"13 (20)","defense":13,"hp":{"value":84,"max":84},"mp":{"value":28,"max":28}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"All Sections","description":""},{"title":"◯ Fire Immunity","description":""},{"title":"Head","description":""},{"title":"► Truespeech Magic , Spiritualism Magic 10 Level/Magic Power 14 (21)","description":""},{"title":"◯ 🗨 ► Magic Aptitude","description":"They can use the Combat Feats [ Targeting ], [ Magic Convergence ], [ Magic Control ], [ Universal Metamagic ], and [ Wordbreak ]."},{"title":"► Flame Breath/15 (22)/Fortitude/Half","description":"With &quot;Range/Area: 2 (20m)/ Shot &quot;, spits fire at &quot;Target: 1 area (6m Radius) / 20&quot;, dealing 2d+20 Fire magic damage.\nThis unique skill cannot be used on consecutive turns."},{"title":"⏩ △ Techniques","description":"They may use the [ Strong Blood ], [ Beetleskin ], and [ Recovery (7 points) ] Techniques."},{"title":"Body","description":""},{"title":"🗨 Tail Sweep","description":"The monster can use its tail to attack up to 5 targets in the same skirmish. An Accuracy check is made on all characters at once, and damage is determined individually.\nThis attack cannot be used in consecutive rounds."},{"title":"◯ Attack Obstacle = Impossible • None","description":"The Lesser Dragon's size hinders attack.\nThe Head cannot be attacked in melee. When the Body falls to 0 HP or lower, this effect disappears."},{"title":"Wing","description":""},{"title":"🗨 All-Out Attack","description":"A Wing can deal an additional 8 damage on its next attack. However, any Evasion check made by this section this turn receives a -3 penalty as a risk."},{"title":"◯ Flight","description":"A Lesser Dragon receives a +1 bonus to Accuracy and Evasion only for melee attacks. If any Wings fall to 0 HP or lower, this unique skill cannot be used."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Dragon Scale (5,000G/Red S)"},{"roll":"2 - 6","loot":"Dragon Fang (1,200G/Red S)"},{"roll":"7 - 12","loot":"Dragon Fang (1,200G/Red S) x 1d"},{"roll":"13+","loot":"Dragon Jewel (10,000G/Gold SS)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Lesser Dragon","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"Idd01UmBufsNtFIn","name":"Pegasus","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:pegasus","level":5,"monsterType":"Mythical Beast","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five senses","disposition":"Neutral","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Mountains","reputation":9,"weakness":16,"weakPoint":"Accuracy +1","initiative":16,"movementSpeed":"20 (4 Legs)/40(Flying)","fortitude":"6 (13)","willpower":"6 (13)","source":"CR III p. 392","description":"A white horse with wings on its back, a Pegasus is a rare sight due to its somewhat skittish personality. The image of a Pegasus is popular in folktales and legends, and it is said that riding one is like running in the sky. They do not simply allow anyone to ride them, so the few adventurers and aristocrats seen on a Pegasus have just that much more prestige.\n\nThe wild species lives mainly in rugged mountains, but it is a popular Mythical Beast for riding and is also kept by the Rider's Guilds. It is rare to find adventurers and nobles who keep them privately.\n\nFor the mount version of this creature, see Pegasus .","combatStyles":[{"style":"Hooves","accuracy":"7 (14)","damage":"2d+5","evasion":"6 (13)","defense":3,"hp":{"value":41,"max":41},"mp":{"value":23,"max":23}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Flight","description":"A Pegasus receives a +1 bonus to Accuracy and Evasion only for melee attacks."},{"title":"◯ Poison/Disease Immunity","description":"When the mount is subjected to a poison or disease-type effect or damage, it can always be resisted as &quot;Resistance: Optional.&quot;"}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"White Feathers (50G/Red B)"},{"roll":"2 - 9","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"10+","loot":"Pure White Mane (800G/Red A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Pegasus","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"J4dgfV6FvGuvDfSi","name":"Varg","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:varg","level":6,"monsterType":"Mythical Beast","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Neutral","soulscars":0,"languages":"Vargian","habitat":"Forests, Plains, Hills","reputation":11,"weakness":16,"weakPoint":"Fire damage + 3 points","initiative":16,"movementSpeed":"20 (4 Legs)","fortitude":"10 (17)","willpower":"8 (15)","source":"Monstrous Lore p. 176","description":"This mythical beast is about 2 meters tall and resembles a huge wolf. Its coat color is a gradation of black to white, with varying degrees of intensity, but mostly gray.\n\nThey have their own language consisting of howls, and they excel at hunting by using it to hunt down their enemies and coordinate their attacks. They are generally belligerent and have a primitive but unique culture centered on hunting.\n\nBecause of the way they are, they joined Dalkhrem's army during the War of the Gods, and even today, they are often seen as friends of the Barbarous, and some of the Barbarous have Varg as their mount. They are especially close to Bolgs , Ogres , Trolls , and Lycanthropes .\n\nThe relationship between Vargs and Barbarous is only as equal partners. It is said that if they are forced to be slaves, they will bite the Barbarous' head off at that moment.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Bite","accuracy":"8 (16)","damage":"2d+8","evasion":"9 (16)","defense":5,"hp":{"value":58,"max":58},"mp":{"value":22,"max":22}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Coordination","description":"A Varg gains a bonus to their Accuracy equal to the number of other Vargs (of any type) in the same skirmish area, up to a maximum of +4."},{"title":"🗨 Power Strike I","description":"A Varg can deal an additional 4 damage on their next attack. However, any Evasion Check made by them this turn receives a -2 penalty."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"2 - 5","loot":"Mythical Beast Hide (140G/Red A)"},{"roll":"6 - 8","loot":"Fine Mythical Beast Hide (300G/Red A)"},{"roll":"9+","loot":"Beautiful Mythical Beast Hide (800G/Gold Red A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Varg","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"JRXrbrf3i0sbWIVy","name":"Afanc","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:afanc","level":10,"monsterType":"Mythical Beast","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five senses","disposition":"Hungry","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Lakes, Wetlands","reputation":10,"weakness":17,"weakPoint":"Physical damage +2 points","initiative":15,"movementSpeed":"18 (4 Legs) / 24 (Swimming)","fortitude":"11 (18)","willpower":"12 (19)","source":"BM","description":"An Afanc is a Mythical Beast that looks like a giant beaver with a somewhat human-like face. It is said to live near lakes and drag all who approach it beneath the waves.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Bite (Head)","accuracy":"13 (20)","damage":"2d+10","evasion":"12 (19)","defense":9,"hp":{"value":92,"max":92},"mp":{"value":54,"max":54}},{"style":"Claws (Body)","accuracy":"14 (21)","damage":"2d+8","evasion":"11 (18)","defense":9,"hp":{"value":98,"max":98},"mp":{"value":35,"max":35}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"All Sections","description":""},{"title":"◯ Underwater Aptitude","description":""},{"title":"Head","description":""},{"title":"⏩ Techniques","description":"They may use the [ Bear Muscle ], [ Cat's Eyes ], and [ Recovery (7 pts.) ] Techniques."},{"title":"Body","description":""},{"title":"► Double Attack","description":"An Afanc can attack the same target twice in one action with its Claws."},{"title":"◯ Hug","description":"The target is grappled if both Claw attacks hit with [ ► Double Attack]. The target will no longer be able to move or make melee or ranged attacks. Also, starting from the next turn, the Body section automatically deals 2d+16 physical damage to the target, and Head section attacks automatically hit the target.\nWhen the target tries to escape, use de-bonding (see ML, p. 71).\nWhile entangled by this unique skill, the Afanc cannot attack other characters. If the monster itself wants to release the target, it can do so with a Minor Action."},{"title":"◯ Attack Obstacle = +4 • None","description":"An Afanc's large size helps prevent enemies from attacking it. The Head receives a +4 bonus to Evasion checks against melee attacks. When the Body falls to 0 HP or lower, this effect disappears."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"2 - 9","loot":"Water-repellent Hide (550G/Red A)"},{"roll":"10+","loot":"Blue-gray Hide (2,200G/Gold Red S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Afanc","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"KAyDG2oP7eZWtLgk","name":"Lemming","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:lemming","level":1,"monsterType":"Mythical Beast","intelligence":"Animal","perception":"Five senses","disposition":"Neutral","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Grassland","reputation":10,"weakness":13,"weakPoint":"Earth damage + 3 points","initiative":7,"movementSpeed":"10 (4 Legs)/-","fortitude":"2 (9)","willpower":"2 (9)","source":"BM","description":"They are adorable mouse-like creatures, about 50cm long. They are rarely seen alone but are sometimes seen crossing grasslands in groups of several hundred.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Bite","accuracy":"2 (9)","damage":"2d-2","evasion":"2 (9)","defense":0,"hp":{"value":10,"max":10},"mp":{"value":10,"max":10}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Swarm","description":"Lemming gains a +1 bonus to Accuracy checks and +1 to HP for each other Lemming in the same skirmish area. The maximum bonus modifier and increase in HP due to this effect are +5."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"2 - 9","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"10+","loot":"Lemming's Tooth (30G/Red B)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Lemming","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"KFLCqLVJ9PPKQeDq","name":"Sky Wyvern","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:sky-wyvern","level":6,"monsterType":"Mythical Beast","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Five senses","disposition":"Neutral","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Mountains","reputation":12,"weakness":17,"weakPoint":"Earth damage +3 points","initiative":15,"movementSpeed":"9/30 (Flying)","fortitude":"9 (16)","willpower":"8 (15)","source":"CO","description":"The Wyvern is a Mythical Beast with a lizard-like head and torso and large wings composed of cortical membranes that allow it to fly. It is sometimes called a &quot;false dragon&quot; because it looks like a dragon, but unlike a dragon, it does not have forelimbs. They also have a low intellect and cannot speak.\n\nThere are many subspecies of Wyverns, differing in size, the type of breath they emit, and whether or not they have a poison stinger on their tail. The Sky Wyvern, common in the Ursyla region, is the smallest of the Wyvern species and is considered relatively easy to control. It is characterized by its shiny, bluish-purple body color.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Bite (Head)","accuracy":"7 (14)","damage":"2d+8","evasion":"7 (14)","defense":6,"hp":{"value":48,"max":48},"mp":{"value":18,"max":18}},{"style":"Claws (Body)","accuracy":"8 (15)","damage":"2d+6","evasion":"6 (13)","defense":7,"hp":{"value":51,"max":51},"mp":{"value":13,"max":13}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"All Sections","description":""},{"title":"◯ Delicate Loot","description":"Whenever an Edged weapon, Wind, or Slashing damage deals 10 or more points of applied damage at any one time, a False Dragon Scale is added to the &quot;Always&quot; obtained loot. This effect is cumulative up to 3 times."},{"title":"Head","description":""},{"title":"► Impact Breath / 8 (15) / Fortitude / Half","description":"With &quot;Range / Area: 2 (30m) / Shot&quot;, the Sky Wyvern spits a wave at &quot;Target: 1 Character&quot;, dealing 2d+6 Bludgeoning magic damage and knocking it prone.\nThis ability cannot be used in consecutive turns."},{"title":"Body","description":""},{"title":"◯ Flight","description":"All sections receive a +1 bonus to Accuracy and Evasion only for melee attacks.\nIf the Body section falls to 0 HP or lower, this unique skill cannot be used."},{"title":"► Twin Strike &amp; Double Attack","description":"It can make two Claws attacks each round, though each attack requires its own Accuracy check. They may choose to attack different characters with each attack."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"False Dragon Scale (350G/Red A)"},{"roll":"2 - 9","loot":"Draconic Patagium (500G/Red A)"},{"roll":"10 - 12","loot":"Blue-Purple Draconic Patagium (1,000G/Red S)"},{"roll":"13+","loot":"Lazuli Draconic Patagium (3,000G/Red S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Sky Wyvern","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"KcAHgkUimtP0CGCn","name":"Thunder Snowbird","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:thunder-snowbird","level":7,"monsterType":"Mythical Beast","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Five senses","disposition":"Hungry","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Mountains, Lakes","reputation":13,"weakness":18,"weakPoint":"Magic Damage +2 points","initiative":16,"movementSpeed":"-/50 (Flying)","fortitude":"10 (17)","willpower":"10 (17)","source":"Natural History of Ursyla p. 133","description":"This is a variant of the Thunderbird observed particularly in the northern part of the Tamir Mountains. It appears during cold periods accompanied by dark clouds, bringing snow and hail along with lightning.\n\nUnlike typical Thunderbirds, its range is more limited, and it is rarely seen outside the Tamir Mountains. However, perhaps because of this, it is highly territorial and will launch fierce attacks against any intruders.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Beak (Body)","accuracy":"9 (16)","damage":"2d+11","evasion":"9 (16)","defense":6,"hp":{"value":49,"max":49},"mp":{"value":26,"max":26}},{"style":"Wing (Wing)","accuracy":"10 (17)","damage":"2d+9","evasion":"8 (15)","defense":4,"hp":{"value":37,"max":37},"mp":{"value":12,"max":12}},{"style":"Wing (Wing)","accuracy":"10 (17)","damage":"2d+9","evasion":"8 (15)","defense":4,"hp":{"value":37,"max":37},"mp":{"value":12,"max":12}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"All Sections","description":""},{"title":"◯ Water/Ice Immunity, ◯ Lightning Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Delicate Loot","description":"If the HP of either Wing section falls to 0 or below, you will only obtain 1 unit of the Loot Strange Flight Feathers. If both Wing sections' HP falls to 0 or below, no Strange Flight Feathers will be obtained."},{"title":"Body","description":""},{"title":"► Thunder Snow / 9 (16) / Willpower / Half","description":"Summons snow and lightning with &quot;Range: Self&quot; and &quot;Target: 1 area (6m radius) / 20&quot; and deals 2d+6 Water/Ice and Lightning magic damage to the target.\nThis ability cannot be used on consecutive turns."},{"title":"Wing","description":""},{"title":"◯ Flight","description":"A Thunderbird receives a +1 bonus to Accuracy and Evasion only for melee attacks.\nIf one of the Wings falls to 0 HP or lower, this unique skill cannot be used."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Strange Flight Feathers (500G/Red A) x 2"},{"roll":"2 - 7","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"8 - 9","loot":"Ice Crystal (1,600G/Gold S)"},{"roll":"10+","loot":"Lightning Crystal (1,600G/Gold S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Thunder Snowbird","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"KxA1H8iXxi0EEC51","name":"Hermit Manticore","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:hermit-manticore","level":8,"monsterType":"Mythical Beast","intelligence":"High","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Neutral","soulscars":0,"languages":"Arcana, Sylvan","habitat":"Labyrinths","reputation":13,"weakness":18,"weakPoint":"Wind damage +3 points","initiative":16,"movementSpeed":"15 (4 Legs)/23 (Flying)","fortitude":"10 (17)","willpower":"11 (18)","source":"BM","description":"This Manticore subspecies knows a deep prophecy about not only magic but also Geomancy . They retreat deep into the mountains and refuse contact with Humanoids and others.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Claw (Front)","accuracy":"11 (18)","damage":"2d+10","evasion":"10 (17)","defense":7,"hp":{"value":77,"max":77},"mp":{"value":51,"max":51}},{"style":"Tail (Rear)","accuracy":"10 (17)","damage":"2d+12","evasion":"9 (16)","defense":5,"hp":{"value":65,"max":65},"mp":{"value":29,"max":29}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"Front","description":""},{"title":"► Truespeech Magic , Spiritualism Magic 7 Level / Magic Power 10 (17)","description":""},{"title":"► Fairy Magic 5 Level / Magic Power 8 (15)","description":"Can use Earth, Fire, Wind, and Dark types.\nThis does not change even if the contract pattern is adopted (see MA, p. 136)."},{"title":"◯ 🗨 Magic Aptitude","description":"They can use the Combat Feats [ Metamagic/Targets ], [ Targeting ], and [ Multi-Action ]."},{"title":"⏩ Aspect/All Areas (20m Radius)","description":"Knows [ Heavenly Domain: Descending Thunder ], [ Earthly Domain: Quicksand ], and [ Spirit Domain: Terror ] Aspects. The Qi Points to be used are all 3 points."},{"title":"Back","description":""},{"title":"◯ Numbing Poison / 10 (17) / Fortitude / Negates","description":"If the Tail's attack hits and deals 1 or more points of applied damage, it has the effect of Petrifaction (Dexterity/-6) (see CR II, p. 329, or ML, p. 71)."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"2 - 7","loot":"Fine Mythical Beast Hide (300G/Red A)"},{"roll":"8+","loot":"Beautiful Mythical Beast Hide (800G/Gold Red A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Hermit Manticore","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"MF26Z0m7gIXHKcuY","name":"Jabberwock","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:jabberwock","level":15,"monsterType":"Mythical Beast","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"Barbaric, Youma, Daemonic, Arcana","habitat":"Forests, Mountains","reputation":19,"weakness":22,"weakPoint":"Silver weapon damage +3 points","initiative":24,"movementSpeed":"20 (4 Legs) / 35 (Flying)","fortitude":"21 (28)","willpower":"19 (26)","source":"BM","description":"The Jabberwock is a mythical beast with a dragon-like head, long neck, four wings, and a long tail, and its total length exceeds 20 meters.\n\nThey are extremely vicious and aggressive. They are also relentless in the pursuit of their prey.\n\nBecause of these characteristics and its use of the Summoning Arts, some believe that Jabberwock is a type of Daemon, while others believe that it originated as a crossbreed between a Daemon and a Dragon.\n\nJabberwocks are found primarily in forests and mountains but may also occur in deserts, wildernesses, and archaeological sites. Often, the habitat of the Jabberwock is oddly tranquil, as there are few other animals.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Bite (Head)","accuracy":"18 (25)","damage":"2d+18","evasion":"20 (27)","defense":15,"hp":{"value":147,"max":147},"mp":{"value":84,"max":84}},{"style":"Claws (Body)","accuracy":"20 (27)","damage":"2d+16","evasion":"16 (23)","defense":16,"hp":{"value":158,"max":158},"mp":{"value":46,"max":46}},{"style":"Wing (Wing)","accuracy":"19 (26)","damage":"2d+12","evasion":"17 (24)","defense":12,"hp":{"value":91,"max":91},"mp":{"value":23,"max":23}},{"style":"Wing (Wing)","accuracy":"19 (26)","damage":"2d+12","evasion":"17 (24)","defense":12,"hp":{"value":91,"max":91},"mp":{"value":23,"max":23}},{"style":"Wing (Wing)","accuracy":"19 (26)","damage":"2d+12","evasion":"17 (24)","defense":12,"hp":{"value":91,"max":91},"mp":{"value":23,"max":23}},{"style":"Wing (Wing)","accuracy":"19 (26)","damage":"2d+12","evasion":"17 (24)","defense":12,"hp":{"value":91,"max":91},"mp":{"value":23,"max":23}},{"style":"Tail (Tail)","accuracy":"21 (28)","damage":"2d+13","evasion":"18 (25)","defense":14,"hp":{"value":142,"max":142},"mp":{"value":32,"max":32}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"Head","description":""},{"title":"► Summoning Arts 15 Level / Magic Power 18 (25)","description":""},{"title":"◯ 🗨 ► Magic Aptitude","description":"They can use the Combat Feats [ Multi-Action ], [ Targeting ], [ Magic Convergence ], [ Magic Control ], [ Hawk Eye ], [ Universal Metamagic , and [ Wordbreak ]."},{"title":"► Shockwave Breath / 20 (27) / Fortitude / Half","description":"Jabberwock breathes a mighty wave with &quot;Range / Area: 2 (30m) / Shot &quot; in a &quot;Target: 1 Area (6m Radius) / 20&quot;, dealing 2d+30 Bludgeoning magic damage to the targets and causing them to fall prone.\nThis ability cannot be used on consecutive turns."},{"title":"Body","description":""},{"title":"◯ Attack Obstacle = +4 • None","description":"Jabberwock's tremendous height prevents enemies from attacking it. The Head section receives a +4 bonus to Evasion checks against melee attacks. When the Body falls to 0 HP or lower, this effect disappears."},{"title":"Wing","description":""},{"title":"🗨 All-Out Attack","description":"A Wing can deal an additional 8 damage on its next attack. However, any Evasion check made by this section this turn receives a -3 penalty."},{"title":"◯ Flight","description":"A Jabberwock receives a +1 bonus to Accuracy and Evasion only for melee attacks.\nIf two Wings fall to 0 HP or lower, this unique skill cannot be used."},{"title":"Tail","description":""},{"title":"🗨 Tail Sweep","description":"A Jabberwock can use its Tail to attack up to 5 targets with a Melee Attack. This attack cannot be used in consecutive rounds."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Shining Red Eyes (5,000G/Gold Red S) x 2"},{"roll":"2 - 6","loot":"Mysterious Scales (1,000G/Red White S)"},{"roll":"7 - 10","loot":"Mysterious Scales (1,000G/Red White S) x 2"},{"roll":"11+","loot":"Mysterious Scales (1,000G/Red White S) x 1d"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Jabberwock","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"NmVfUkdPSTu0sZyt","name":"Chimera","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:chimera","level":9,"monsterType":"Mythical Beast","intelligence":"High","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"Trade Common, Barbaric, Dragonic, Arcana","habitat":"Ruins","reputation":13,"weakness":20,"weakPoint":"Magic damage +2 points","initiative":15,"movementSpeed":"13 (4 Legs)/25 (Flying)","fortitude":"11 (18)","willpower":"12 (19)","source":"CR II p. 393","description":"Chimera is fearsome in appearance, with the heads of a lion, goat, and dragon, the body of a snake used for a tail, and the wings of a massive bat on its back. Their origin is unclear, but it can only be assumed that a crazed wizard from the Magic Civilization period came up with this beast as part of some deranged experiment.\n\nWith multiple heads comes incredible intelligence, and Chimeras excel in cunning strategy. They are also ruthless and will offer hope to their opponents only to snatch it away at the last second. Chimeras also tend to have Undead and Constructs under their control and will have each head sleep at different times, making them formidable opponents to take advantage of. However, Chimeras tend to be overconfident, and it is said that this hubris may be their downfall.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Bite (Lion's Head)","accuracy":"11 (18)","damage":"2d+13","evasion":"10 (17)","defense":9,"hp":{"value":81,"max":81},"mp":{"value":12,"max":12}},{"style":"Horn (Goat's Head)","accuracy":"9 (16)","damage":"2d+9","evasion":"10 (17)","defense":8,"hp":{"value":68,"max":68},"mp":{"value":60,"max":60}},{"style":"Bite (Dragon's Head)","accuracy":"10 (17)","damage":"2d+11","evasion":"10 (17)","defense":10,"hp":{"value":74,"max":74},"mp":{"value":18,"max":18}},{"style":"Snake's Bite (Body)","accuracy":"12 (19)","damage":"2d+9","evasion":"11 (18)","defense":6,"hp":{"value":87,"max":87},"mp":{"value":12,"max":12}},{"style":"None (Wings)","accuracy":"-","damage":"-","evasion":"9 (16)","defense":8,"hp":{"value":59,"max":59},"mp":{"value":12,"max":12}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"Lion's Head","description":""},{"title":"⏩ △ Techniques","description":"They may use the [ Cat's Eyes ], [ Beetleskin ], and [ Recovery (5 points) ] Techniques."},{"title":"Goat's Head","description":""},{"title":"► Spiritualism Magic 7 Level/Magic Power 10 (17)","description":""},{"title":"◯ 🗨 ► Magic Aptitude","description":"They can use the Combat Feats [ Targeting ], [ Magic Convergence ], [ Magic Control ], [ Universal Metamagic ], and [ Wordbreak ]."},{"title":"Dragon's Head","description":""},{"title":"► Flame Breath/11 (18)/Fortitude/Half","description":"With &quot;Range/Area: 2 (50m) / Shot &quot;, it spits fire at &quot;Target: 1 Character&quot; and deals 2d+10 Fire magic damage."},{"title":"Body","description":""},{"title":"◯ Cursed Poison/11 (18)/Fortitude/Negates","description":"If the Snake's Bite attack hits and deals at least 1 point of applied damage, the target's Accuracy check will be reduced by -2. This effect is not cumulative.\nThis effect is treated as a Curse type and is permanent. This effect can be removed with a spell such as [ Remove Curse ], but it is also automatically removed if the Body section of the Chimera that bestowed the curse falls to 0 HP or less."},{"title":"Wings","description":""},{"title":"◯ Flight","description":"A Chimera receives a +1 bonus to Accuracy and Evasion only for melee attacks. If Wings falls to 0 HP or lower, this unique skill cannot be used."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Chimera Horn (500G/Red A)"},{"roll":"Always","loot":"Chimera Fang (500G/Red A)"},{"roll":"2 - 9","loot":"Chimera Mane (500G/Red A)"},{"roll":"10+","loot":"Golden Chimera Mane (2,900G/Gold Red S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Chimera","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"NsnOg0WPQbP5JH14","name":"Amethyst Tapir","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:amethyst-tapir","level":7,"monsterType":"Mythical Beast","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Neutral","soulscars":0,"languages":"Trade Common, Daemonic","habitat":"Forests, Lakes, Shallows","reputation":15,"weakness":18,"weakPoint":"Fire damage +3 points","initiative":14,"movementSpeed":"14 (4 Legs)","fortitude":"9 (16)","willpower":"10 (17)","source":"AB, p. 117","description":"This is a Mythical Beast resembling a tapir with purple fur. It has the ability to feed on the delusions and nightmares of intelligent beings, and perhaps because of this, it seems to feel most at home in a Shallow Abyss, which could be described as a space where delusions materialize. It is known for frequent sightings in the Shallows, where it attempts to put Humanoids and Barbarous who enter the Shallow to sleep to feed on their dreams.\n\nDue to its conflict-averse nature, it typically tries to negotiate friendly terms by suggesting short periods like one or two days for sleep, but if refused, it will attempt to force sleep upon its targets. In such cases, one might end up having their dreams eaten for quite a long time.\n\nRarely, while using its [Dream Eater] ability, an Amethyst Tapir will take direct part within the victim's dream. When it does, its dream avatar appears as a pleasant-voiced Humanoid nurse with tapir-like ears. This form uses a pipe to &quot;smoke&quot; any nightmarish images, leaving behind only pleasant dreams.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Nose","accuracy":"9(16)","damage":"2d+6","evasion":"&#32;","defense":6,"hp":{"value":6,"max":6},"mp":{"value":32,"max":32}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"► Abyssal Magic 7 Level / Magic Power 9 (16)","description":"Enhanced effects can be used up to 2 rounds."},{"title":"◯🗨►Magic Aptitude","description":"They can use Combat Feats [ Targeting ], [ Magic Convergence ], [ Magic Control ], [ Hawk Eye ], [ Universal Metamagic ], and [ Wordbreak ]."},{"title":"◯Shallow Aptitude","description":"Within a Shallow Abyss, all sections receive a +1 bonus to all skill check results."},{"title":"►Luring to Dreams / 8 (15) / Willpower / Negates","description":"Within &quot;Range/Area: 2 (30m) / Target &quot;, puts &quot;Target: 1 Entire Character&quot; to sleep. This effect is Curse + Psychic (Weak) type. It follows the rules for Curse + Psychic effects (see CR II, p. 128, or MA, p. 75), but when calculating resistance, consider immunity to &quot;Psychic (Weak)&quot; rather than &quot;Psychic.&quot;\nThis effect lasts for up to 100 years (during which time the target needs no food, drink, or excretion, and does not age), though in most cases, this monster will release the target before completion (see [►Dream Eater]). Alternatively, the effect is dispelled if this monster's HP falls to 0 or below."},{"title":"►Dream Eater / Can't","description":"This effect can only target characters that have either PC data or monster data with Intellect: Low/Average/High, or an equivalent/higher intelligence as determined by the GM.\nFurthermore, it cannot be used unless the target is already asleep. Usage requires 1 hour, and if the target wakes up during this time, they become immune to this effect. Therefore, in most cases, characters who have been put to sleep by [►Luring to Dreams] become the targets of this effect.\nWith &quot;Range: Touch&quot; and &quot;Target: 1 Entire Character&quot;, it consumes the dreams the target is seeing. This reduces the target's Spirit by 1d points. If a character's spirit reaches &quot;0&quot; through this effect, they die and cannot be resurrected. For characters with monster data, this death does not occur.\nThis Spirit change recovers automatically by &quot;1&quot; point per day.\nThe Amethyst Tapir desires to continuously eat dreams. Therefore, they generally do not use this effect to the point of the death of their targets. They try to continue feeding by determining a safe range for their &quot;meals.&quot;\nWhile the [►Luring to Dreams] effect brings 100 years of sleep, in most cases, an Amethyst Tapir gets tired of that character's taste before that time is up. In such cases, the Amethyst Tapir irresponsibly dispels the effect after throwing the sleeping victims away from its lair (and sometimes out of the Shallow Abyss completely). As a result, these individuals wake up bewildered, finding themselves cast away in unfamiliar lands and times."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"2 - 5","loot":"Mythical Beast Hide (140G/Red A)"},{"roll":"6 - 7","loot":"Fine Mythical Beast Hide (300G/Red A)"},{"roll":"8 - 10","loot":"Beautiful Mythical Beast Hide (800G/Gold Red A)"},{"roll":"11+","loot":"Magnificent Mythical Beast Hide (2,100G/Gold Red S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Amethyst Tapir","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"OqsZKLD5ZXYhC5bj","name":"Dragon Infant","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:dragon-infant","level":4,"monsterType":"Mythical Beast","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Neutral","soulscars":0,"languages":"Dragonic","habitat":"Various","reputation":12,"weakness":15,"weakPoint":"Physical damage +2 points","initiative":12,"movementSpeed":"10/20 (Flying)","fortitude":"6 (13)","willpower":"5 (12)","source":"BM","description":"This is a baby dragon at least 30 years old and is still in its early stages of development. At this age, they rarely leave their parents and are rarely seen flying in the sky with others.\n\nIt is not as majestic as a fully-grown dragon due to its low intelligence, but it is still considered more of a threat than most monsters. Furthermore, there is a high probability that their parents are nearby, and they will often flee to them when in danger.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Bite","accuracy":"5 (12)","damage":"2d+6","evasion":"4 (11)","defense":3,"hp":{"value":33,"max":33},"mp":{"value":20,"max":20}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"► Fire Breath / 5 (12) / Fortitude / Half","description":"A Dragon Infant breathes fire in a &quot;Range / Area:2 (20m) / Shot &quot; to the &quot;Target: 1 Character&quot;, dealing 2d + 4 Fire magic damage.\nThis unique skill cannot be used in consecutive rounds."},{"title":"◯ Flight","description":"A Dragon Infant receives a +1 bonus to Accuracy and Evasion only for melee attacks."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"2 - 11","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"12+","loot":"Dragon Fang (1,200G/Red S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Dragon Infant","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"TduoUBngQLEM07pW","name":"Tilgris","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:tilgris","level":8,"monsterType":"Mythical Beast","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five senses","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Forests, Mountains","reputation":14,"weakness":17,"weakPoint":"Slashing damage +3 points","initiative":16,"movementSpeed":"30(Legs)","fortitude":"11 (18)","willpower":"10 (17)","source":"CR III p. 394","description":"A Tilgris is a Mythical Beast similar to a tiger, with red and black tiger stripes on its fur. However, it is two times larger than an ordinary tiger.\n\nIt is characterized by a partially hardened skin from the forehead to the back that makes it appear armored. Tilgris, in addition to its sharp fangs and claws, uses its tail skillfully and mercilessly to attack its enemies. In addition, Tilgris has the ability to spit lightning breath, which has been described as &quot;like a lightning cloud descending directly from the sky.&quot;\n\nThey are territorial and exclusive, and it is considered very dangerous to venture into their territory.\n\nAlthough they are often regarded as violent because of their ecology, they are also known to be as intelligent as humans. Although they cannot speak, they can understand human languages and are not easy to trap.\n\nOn the other hand, they are also known to be very faithful to their fellow humanoids, and some of them have developed friendships with humanoids and act as mounts in the Rider's Guilds.\n\nFor the mount version of this creature, see Tilgris .","combatStyles":[{"style":"Claws (Front)","accuracy":"11 (18)","damage":"2d+8","evasion":"11 (18)","defense":8,"hp":{"value":69,"max":69},"mp":{"value":24,"max":24}},{"style":"Tail (Back)","accuracy":"10 (17)","damage":"2d+10","evasion":"10 (17)","defense":8,"hp":{"value":77,"max":77},"mp":{"value":12,"max":12}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"Front","description":""},{"title":"► Double Attack","description":"Can make two Claws attacks with one Major Action."},{"title":"► Lightning Breath/10 (17)/Fortitude/Half","description":"It spits lightning with &quot;Range/Area: 2 (20m) / Shot &quot; to &quot;Target: 1 area (3m Radius) / 5.&quot; It deals 2d+9 Lightning and Water/Ice magic damage.\nThis ability cannot be used on consecutive turns."},{"title":"Back","description":""},{"title":"◯ Long Tail","description":"Tail attacks can be made with &quot;Range/Area: 1 (10m) / Target &quot;."},{"title":"◯ Painful Strike","description":"If their 2d damage roll is 10 or more, the damage is increased by an additional +7 points."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"2 - 6","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"7 - 11","loot":"Hard Outer Skin (800G/Red A)"},{"roll":"12+","loot":"Shiny Hard Outer Skin (2,600G/Red S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Tilgris","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"Tgt0joW3JB81bu8Q","name":"Peryton","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:peryton","level":6,"monsterType":"Mythical Beast","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Shallows","reputation":11,"weakness":16,"weakPoint":"Wind-type damage +3 points","initiative":14,"movementSpeed":"18 (4 Legs) / 30 (Flying)","fortitude":"9 (16)","willpower":"9 (16)","source":"AB, p. 116","description":"A Peryton is a Mythical Beast that takes the form of a deer with raptor wings, tail feathers, and a majestic branching horn. Though it possesses a divine and dignified appearance, it is considered an ominous symbol due to its power to bring misfortune to those around it.\n\nThere are legends of Peryton sightings as far back as the formation of the Abyss, with a history of active efforts to exterminate them. To escape from hunters, Perytons fled into Shallow Abysses. As a result, they are rarely seen outside of the Shallows.\n\nDue to their past, they harbor hatred toward Humanoids and Barbarous, actively attacking them on sight.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Big Horns","accuracy":"8(15)","damage":"2d+7","evasion":"&#32;","defense":8,"hp":{"value":5,"max":5},"mp":{"value":32,"max":32}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯Flight","description":"Gains a +1 bonus to Accuracy checks and Evasion checks for melee attacks."},{"title":"◯Field of Misfortune","description":"With &quot;Range: Caster&quot; and &quot;Target: All areas (30m radius) / Space&quot;, it creates a field of misfortune. Within the effect range, any skill check performed by creatures other than this monster will result in automatic failure if either die in the 2d roll is a &quot;1&quot;. This effect does not apply to rolls on the Power Table.\nWhen other monsters exist and use fixed values, the GM rolls 1d for each instance of using a fixed value. On a roll of &quot;1&quot;, it is treated as an automatic failure. On rolls of &quot;2-6&quot;, the fixed value is used as normal.\nNo experience points are gained from automatic failures caused by this effect."},{"title":"🗨Horn of Resentment","description":"Attacks with the Big Horns inflict Curse magic damage when they hit. However, Accuracy checks receive a -1 penalty, and the damage is reduced by -2."},{"title":"◯Regeneration = 3 points (Shallow)","description":"At the end of its turn, HP recovers by 3 points. This effect only appears when this monster is inside a Shallow Abyss.\nWhen HP reaches 0 or below, this ability is lost."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Flight Feathers (100G/Red A)"},{"roll":"2 - 9","loot":"Broken Horn (30G/Red B)"},{"roll":"10+","loot":"Dangerous Horns (1,000G/Red S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Peryton","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"Ug65jgPOsvXlvc3Z","name":"Chimera Summoner","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:chimera-summoner","level":11,"monsterType":"Mythical Beast","intelligence":"High","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"Trade Common, Barbaric, Arcana, Daemonic","habitat":"Ruins, Shallow Abysses","reputation":16,"weakness":22,"weakPoint":"Magic damage +2 points","initiative":17,"movementSpeed":"13 (4 Legs)/25 (Flying)","fortitude":"13 (20)","willpower":"14 (21)","source":"Natural History of Ursyla p. 134","description":"This peculiar Mythical Beast has been sighted near the borders of the Zamsaska region.\n\nIt has the heads of a lion and a goat, with a snake for a tail and membrane-like wings. While clearly a subspecies of the Mythical Beast Chimera , instead of having a dragon's head, it features a prominently large goat head.\n\nThis goat head is specialized in using Summoning Arts , and it is believed that such modifications and adjustments were made during the Ancient Magic Civilization era. The Chimera Summoner seems to favor this ability, actively summoning Daemons and letting them roam freely.\n\nThe Chimera Summoner is believed to lurk in ruins from the Ancient Magic Civilization era in the northern territory of the Holy Iron Chain Principality of Sukhbaar. Additionally, it appears to have the ability to enter and exit the Shallow Abyss, as encounters within the Shallow have been reported. When cornered, there are instances of it teleporting to the Shallow Abyss, making it rather elusive.\n\nIn combat, it often brings Daemons as guards, making it even more dangerous. The Chimera Summoner possesses a special black gem for entering the Shallow Abyss, where it hides, allowing it to jump into Shallow areas even from distant locations (see Natural History of Ursyla p. 40).","combatStyles":[{"style":"Bite (Lion's Head)","accuracy":"13 (20)","damage":"2d+16","evasion":"12 (19)","defense":10,"hp":{"value":98,"max":98},"mp":{"value":15,"max":15}},{"style":"Horn (Goat's Head)","accuracy":"11 (18)","damage":"2d+12","evasion":"12 (19)","defense":10,"hp":{"value":103,"max":103},"mp":{"value":76,"max":76}},{"style":"Snake's Bite (Body)","accuracy":"14 (21)","damage":"2d+12","evasion":"13 (20)","defense":7,"hp":{"value":107,"max":107},"mp":{"value":15,"max":15}},{"style":"Wings (Wings)","accuracy":"12 (19)","damage":"2d+11","evasion":"11 (18)","defense":9,"hp":{"value":74,"max":74},"mp":{"value":15,"max":15}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"Lion's Head","description":""},{"title":"⏩ △ Techniques","description":"They may use the [ Cat's Eyes ], [ Beetleskin ], and [ Recovery (5 points) ] Techniques."},{"title":"Goat's Head","description":""},{"title":"► Summoning Arts 10 Level / Magic Power 13 (20)","description":""},{"title":"◯ 🗨 ► Magic Aptitude","description":"They can use the Combat Feats [ Multi-Action ], [ Targeting ], [ Magic Convergence ], [ Magic Control ], [ Universal Metamagic ], and [ Wordbreak ]."},{"title":"Body","description":""},{"title":"◯ Cursed Poison / 13 (20) / Fortitude / Negates","description":"If the Snake's Bite attack hits and deals at least 1 point of applied damage, the target's Accuracy check will be reduced by -2. This effect is not cumulative.\nThis effect is treated as a Curse type and is permanent. This effect can be removed with a spell such as [ Remove Curse ], but it is also automatically removed if the Body section of the Chimera that bestowed the curse falls to 0 HP or less."},{"title":"Wings","description":""},{"title":"◯ Flight","description":"A Chimera receives a +1 bonus to Accuracy and Evasion only for melee attacks. If Wings falls to 0 HP or lower, this unique skill cannot be used."},{"title":"All Sections","description":""},{"title":"◯Delicate Loot","description":"The Abyssal Blackstone loot can only be obtained once. Any subsequent acquisitions will be changed to Golden Chimera Mane."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Chimera Horn (500G/Red A)"},{"roll":"Always","loot":"Chimera Fang (500G/Red A)"},{"roll":"2 - 7","loot":"Chimera Mane (500G/Red A)"},{"roll":"8 - 11","loot":"Golden Chimera Mane (2,900G/Gold Red S)"},{"roll":"12+","loot":"Abyssal Blackstone (6,000G/Gold Black S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Chimera Summoner","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"WZvFr1yRv0chd2hu","name":"Greater Dragon","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:greater-dragon","level":18,"monsterType":"Mythical Beast","intelligence":"High","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Neutral","soulscars":0,"languages":"Trade Common, Dragonic, Arcana","habitat":"Mountains, Caves","reputation":18,"weakness":24,"weakPoint":"Physical damage +2 points","initiative":23,"movementSpeed":"20/40(Flying)","fortitude":"24 (31)","willpower":"24 (31)","source":"CR III p. 399","description":"This is a mature dragon, about 2,000 years old. Its total length is nearly 20 meters, and its strength rivals that of the armies of great nations. For this reason, most people think of them more like a natural disaster than an enemy to be defeated.\n\nThey are sensitive and will not tolerate any interference. They will direct all of their dragon clan to destroy unwanted intruders if they come to their territory uninvited.\n\nThey are also well known in history and magic but often cannot remember the details of incredibly old matters and may add fictional details to fill those gaps.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Bite (Head)","accuracy":"23 (30)","damage":"2d+21","evasion":"24 (31)","defense":17,"hp":{"value":170,"max":170},"mp":{"value":102,"max":102}},{"style":"Claws (Body)","accuracy":"24 (31)","damage":"2d+19","evasion":"21 (28)","defense":19,"hp":{"value":182,"max":182},"mp":{"value":132,"max":132}},{"style":"Wing (Wing)","accuracy":"21 (28)","damage":"2d+17","evasion":"22 (29)","defense":14,"hp":{"value":126,"max":126},"mp":{"value":81,"max":81}},{"style":"Wing (Wing)","accuracy":"22 (29)","damage":"2d+17","evasion":"22 (29)","defense":14,"hp":{"value":126,"max":126},"mp":{"value":81,"max":81}},{"style":"Tail (Tail)","accuracy":"22 (29)","damage":"2d+19","evasion":"22 (29)","defense":18,"hp":{"value":166,"max":166},"mp":{"value":94,"max":94}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"All Sections","description":""},{"title":"◯ Energy Immunity, ◯ Fire Immunity","description":""},{"title":"Head","description":""},{"title":"► Truespeech Magic , Spiritualism Magic 15 Level/Magic Power 20 (27)","description":""},{"title":"◯ 🗨 ► Magic Aptitude","description":"The Greater Dragon can use the Combat Feats [ Multi-Action ], [ Targeting ], [ Magic Convergence ], [ Magic Control ], [ Universal Metamagic ], and [ Rune Master ]."},{"title":"► Flame and Brilliant Breath/22 (29)/ Fortitude/Half","description":"Within &quot;Range/Area: 2 (50m) / Shot &quot;, spits out breath to &quot;Target: 1 area (6m Radius)/20&quot; and deals magic damage to the target. In this case, the monster can arbitrarily choose one of the following two types, which differ in damage and type.\nFlame Breath: Spits out fire, dealing 2d+30 Fire type.\nBrilliant Breath: Spits out an energy mass, dealing 2d+24 Energy type.\nThis ability cannot be used in consecutive turns (whichever breath is used, neither breath can be used in the next turn)."},{"title":"Body","description":""},{"title":"◯ 2 Actions","description":"Can perform two Major Actions in one round."},{"title":"► Wordbreak","description":"Greater Dragon uses [ Wordbreak ] combat feat using Head's Magic Power."},{"title":"◯ Attack Obstacle = Impossible • None","description":"The Greater Dragon's size hinders attacks.\nThe Head of the Greater Dragon cannot be attacked with melee attacks. This unique skill is lost when the Body section has 0 or less HP."},{"title":"Wing","description":""},{"title":"◯ Flight II","description":"All sections receive a +2 bonus to Accuracy and Evasion only for melee attacks.\nIf one of the Wings falls to 0 HP or lower, this unique skill cannot be used."},{"title":"🗨 All-Out Attack","description":"A Wing can deal an additional 8 damage on its next attack. However, any Evasion check made by this section this turn receives a -3 penalty."},{"title":"Tail","description":""},{"title":"🗨 Tail Sweep","description":"The monster can use its tail to attack up to 5 targets in the same skirmish. An Accuracy check is made on all characters at once, and damage is determined individually.\nThis attack cannot be used in consecutive rounds."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Dragon Fang (1,200G/Red S) x 1d"},{"roll":"Always","loot":"Dragon Scale (5,000G/Red S)"},{"roll":"2 - 9","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"10+","loot":"Dragon Jewel (10,000G/Gold SS)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Greater Dragon","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"WwnpbPYJg5jmYMei","name":"Elder Dragon","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:elder-dragon","level":25,"monsterType":"Mythical Beast","intelligence":"High","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Neutral","soulscars":0,"languages":"Trade Common, Dragonic, Arcana","habitat":"Mountains, Caves","reputation":10,"weakness":33,"weakPoint":"Physical damage +2 points","initiative":35,"movementSpeed":"30/60(Flying)","fortitude":"29 (36)","willpower":"29 (36)","source":"Monstrous Lore p. 185","description":"This is a legendary dragon. Its age ranges from several thousand to tens of thousands of years old, and although it is still alive, its references can be found in histories and myths of ages past. It is more like a divine being than a mythical beast, and is comparable to a Minor God, as they can be worshiped in some areas.\n\nIf anyone ever manages to defeat it, this deed will be passed down from generation to generation.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Bite (Head)","accuracy":"32 (39)","damage":"2d+29","evasion":"32 (39)","defense":28,"hp":{"value":254,"max":254},"mp":{"value":201,"max":201}},{"style":"Claws (Body)","accuracy":"33 (40)","damage":"2d+27","evasion":"30 (37)","defense":30,"hp":{"value":323,"max":323},"mp":{"value":167,"max":167}},{"style":"Wing (Wing)","accuracy":"30 (37)","damage":"2d+26","evasion":"31 (38)","defense":25,"hp":{"value":180,"max":180},"mp":{"value":98,"max":98}},{"style":"Wing (Wing)","accuracy":"30 (37)","damage":"2d+26","evasion":"31 (38)","defense":25,"hp":{"value":180,"max":180},"mp":{"value":98,"max":98}},{"style":"Tail (Tail)","accuracy":"31 (38)","damage":"2d+27","evasion":"31 (38)","defense":29,"hp":{"value":286,"max":286},"mp":{"value":125,"max":125}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"All Sections","description":""},{"title":"◯ Energy Immunity, ◯ Fire Immunity","description":""},{"title":"Head","description":""},{"title":"► Truespeech Magic , Spiritualism Magic 15 Level/Magic Power 28 (35)","description":""},{"title":"◯ 🗨 Magic Aptitude &amp; Breath Aptitude","description":"The Elder Dragon can use the Combat Feats [ Multi-Action ], [ Targeting ], [ Magic Convergence ], [ Magic Control ], [ Universal Metamagic ], and [ Rune Master ].\nWhen declaring [ Multi-Action ], it can select not only the combination of &quot;Melee Attack and Spell Cast&quot; but also the combination of &quot;Melee Attack, [ ► Flame and Brilliant Breath], or &quot;Spell Cast and [ ► Flame and Brilliant Breath]&quot; with one Major Action."},{"title":"► Flame and Brilliant Breath/28 (35)/ Fortitude/Half","description":"Within &quot;Range/Area: 2 (50m) / Shot &quot;, it spits out breath to &quot;Target: 1 area (6m Radius) / 20&quot; and deals magic damage to the target. In this case, the monster can arbitrarily choose one of the following two types, which differ in damage and type.\nFlame Breath: Spits out fire, dealing 2d+40 Fire type.\nBrilliant Breath: Spits out an energy mass, dealing 2d+30 Energy type.\nThis ability cannot be used in consecutive turns (whichever breath is used, neither breath can be used in the next turn)."},{"title":"Body","description":""},{"title":"► Wordbreak","description":"Elder Dragon uses [ Wordbreak ] combat feat using Head's Magic Power."},{"title":"◯ Attack Obstacle = Impossible • None, Magic Obstacle = -4","description":"The Elder Dragon's huge body poking through the clouds hinders the attack.\nThe Head of the Greater Dragon cannot be engaged in melee combat. And if a character casts a spell targeting the Head section or other character in the same section caster gains a -4 penalty on the Spellcasting check.\nThis unique skill is lost when the Body section has 0 or less HP."},{"title":"Wing","description":""},{"title":"◯ Flight II","description":"All sections receive a +2 bonus to Accuracy and Evasion only for melee attacks.\nIf one of the Wings falls to 0 HP or lower, this unique skill cannot be used."},{"title":"🗨 All-Out Attack","description":"A Wing can deal an additional 8 damage on its next attack. However, any Evasion check made by this section this turn receives a -3 penalty."},{"title":"Tail","description":""},{"title":"► Sweeping Attack","description":"Elder Dragon makes a Tail attack against all enemies in the same skirmish.\nThis unique skill cannot be used on consecutive turns."},{"title":"🗨 Improved Aimed Attack","description":"When attacking, the Elder Dragon can gain a +4 bonus to Accuracy but receives a -8 penalty for damage dealt.\nThis cannot be declared when performing an [ ► Sweeping Attack]."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Dragon Fang (1,200G/Red S) x 2d"},{"roll":"Always","loot":"Dragon Scale (5,000G/Red S)"},{"roll":"2 - 13","loot":"Dragon Jewel (10,000G/Gold SS)"},{"roll":"14+","loot":"Greater Dragon Jewel (50,000G/Gold SS)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Elder Dragon","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"awOHNNxcfTU8srCm","name":"Phantasmal Butterfly","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:phantasmal-butterfly","level":7,"monsterType":"Mythical Beast","intelligence":"High","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Neutral","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Forest, Lakeside","reputation":15,"weakness":18,"weakPoint":"Physical damage +2 points","initiative":14,"movementSpeed":"-/10 (Floating)","fortitude":"9 (16)","willpower":"9 (16)","source":"BM","description":"This is a large butterfly, about 3 meters long. Its wings are beautifully iridescent and it flies slowly in the sky.\n\nAlthough they do not speak a language, they are able to share their thoughts with others, and may act as mediators in their territory.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Proboscis (Body)","accuracy":"9 (16)","damage":"2d+7","evasion":"9 (16)","defense":5,"hp":{"value":48,"max":48},"mp":{"value":48,"max":48}},{"style":"Wings (Right Wing)","accuracy":"10 (17)","damage":"2d+8","evasion":"8 (15)","defense":4,"hp":{"value":52,"max":52},"mp":{"value":33,"max":33}},{"style":"Wings (Left Wing)","accuracy":"10 (17)","damage":"2d+8","evasion":"8 (15)","defense":4,"hp":{"value":52,"max":52},"mp":{"value":33,"max":33}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"Body","description":""},{"title":"◯ Mana Absorption Proboscis / 8 (15) / Fortitude / Negates","description":"A target whose HP is reduced by a Proboscis attack has its MP reduced by 1d points. At the same time, the MP of the Body section is recovered by the same amount."},{"title":"◯ 🗨 Magic Aptitude","description":"They can use the Combat Feats [ Targeting ], [ Metamagic/Targets ], and [ Multi-Action ]."},{"title":"► Fairy Magic 7 Level / Magic Power 10 (17)","description":"Can use Earth, Water/Ice, Wind, and Light types.\nThis does not change even if the contract pattern is adopted (see MA, p. 136)."},{"title":"Right Wing/Left Wing","description":""},{"title":"◯ Light Protection","description":"The Right Wing and Left Wing take -3 less magic damage, regardless of type."},{"title":"◯ Adhesive Scales","description":"If a melee attack with an edged weapon hits a Right Wing or Left Wing section, the physical damage dealt by the weapon is reduced by 1 point immediately after the attack. This effect is cumulative (up to -4). This effect lasts until the weapon is cleaned with more than 10 liters of fresh water for 10 minutes."},{"title":"► Phantasmal Scales / 9 (16) / Willpower / Negates","description":"Within &quot;Range: Touch,&quot; confuses &quot;Target: 1 Entire Character&quot; and makes it difficult to recognize the enemy. When a target uses a melee attack or casts a spell targeting the Body section within the next 10 seconds (1 round), roll 1d. If the result is &quot;1-3&quot;, the target will be automatically switched to the section that used this unique skill. If the result is &quot;4-6&quot;, the target will remain in the Body section without any change.\nThis effect does not work if the Body section is only one of multiple targets from [ Metamagic/Targets ].\nThis effect is treated as a Psychic type."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"2 - 7","loot":"Butterfly Scales (100G/Red A)"},{"roll":"8 - 10","loot":"Glittering Scales (300G/Red A)"},{"roll":"12+","loot":"Dazzling Scales (600G/Gold Red A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Phantasmal Butterfly","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"bM5anUNXNhNQ447a","name":"Amphisbaena","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:amphisbaena","level":7,"monsterType":"Mythical Beast","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Cave, Cold Region, Alpine","reputation":12,"weakness":18,"weakPoint":"Magic damage +2 points","initiative":14,"movementSpeed":"20 (Rotation)","fortitude":"10 (17)","willpower":"9 (16)","source":"CR III p. 393","description":"This is a two-headed poison snake with a head at each end of its body. It has bat-like wings, but they are small and degenerate, and it cannot fly. It moves by rolling around like a wheel, with one head clamped onto the other.\n\nIn addition to having a poisonous bite, it is also known to breathe poisonous gas, Some scholars believe that, like Wyverns, it may have some connection to dragons.\n\nPreferring cold climates, they mainly live in caves. There, they wait for prey to wander in, kill them with poisonous gas, and devour them.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Bite (Head)","accuracy":"10 (17)","damage":"2d+9","evasion":"9 (16)","defense":7,"hp":{"value":42,"max":42},"mp":{"value":19,"max":19}},{"style":"Bite (Head)","accuracy":"10 (17)","damage":"2d+9","evasion":"9 (16)","defense":7,"hp":{"value":42,"max":42},"mp":{"value":19,"max":19}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"All Sections","description":""},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity","description":""},{"title":"Head","description":""},{"title":"◯ Poison/10 (17)/Fortitude/Negates","description":"If the Bite hits, it deals 8 poison magic damage to the target."},{"title":"► Poisonous Gas Breath/10 (17)/Fortitude/Half","description":"Within &quot;Range/Area: 2 (20m)/ Shot &quot; spits out poison gas in &quot;1 area (3m Radius) / 5&quot;, dealing 2d Poison magic damage to the targets.\nThis ability cannot be used for consecutive turns."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"2 - 4","loot":"Snake Skin (20G/Red B)"},{"roll":"5 - 7","loot":"Fine Snake Skin (120G/Red A)"},{"roll":"8 - 11","loot":"Premium Snake Skin (320G/Red A)"},{"roll":"12+","loot":"Mythical Snake Skin (1,600G/Red S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Amphisbaena","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"bqtfJYvAIK1NnF5i","name":"Al-Mi'raj","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:almiraj","level":2,"monsterType":"Mythical Beast","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Five senses","disposition":"Hungry","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Forests, Plains, Mountains","reputation":10,"weakness":13,"weakPoint":"Physical damage +2 points","initiative":8,"movementSpeed":"15 (4 Legs)/-","fortitude":"4 (11)","willpower":"3 (10)","source":"BM","description":"Al-Mi'raj is a mythical beast in the shape of a rabbit about 50cm long with a single sharp horn on its head. Using its magic power, it catches prey animals off guard, skewers them with its sharp horn, and then feeds on them. Sometimes, a human who approaches the animal may be fooled by the animal's charm and become a victim.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Horn","accuracy":"4 (11)","damage":"2d+2","evasion":"5 (12)","defense":1,"hp":{"value":20,"max":20},"mp":{"value":13,"max":13}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Lovely Eyes / 4 (11) / Willpower / Negates","description":"A character who sees Al-Mi'raj at the start of their turn must make a Willpower check. If they fail, they will be less hostile and receive a -2 penalty to their Accuracy check for the next 10 seconds (1 round).\nA character who has received 1 or more points of applied damage from Al-Mi'raj will not be affected by this unique skill for a period of one day. Also, this effect is Psychic type."},{"title":"🗨 Power Strike I","description":"They can deal an additional 4 damage on their next attack. However, any Evasion Check made by them this turn receives a -2 penalty."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"2 - 7","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"8 - 10","loot":"Fur (150G/Red A)"},{"roll":"11+","loot":"Al-Mi'raj Horn (300G/Red A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Al-Mi'raj","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"cmlbRcJEOpWNLGHQ","name":"Tarrasque","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:tarrasque","level":12,"monsterType":"Mythical Beast","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Neutral","soulscars":0,"languages":"Dragonic","habitat":"Oceans, Lakes","reputation":19,"weakness":22,"weakPoint":"Physical damage +2 points","initiative":17,"movementSpeed":"14 (Many Legs) / 21 (Swimming)","fortitude":"16 (23)","willpower":"15 (22)","source":"Natural History of Dorden p. 131","description":"Tarrasque is a Mythical Beast about 5 meters in length that can be rarely seen in lakeside and coastal areas of the Dorden region. Although considered a subspecies of dragon, it has no wings and carries a huge turtle-like shell with large spikes. Additionally, it has a mane on its head similar to that of a Lion, and six legs with sharp, long claws and a long, flexible tail.\n\nWhile it doesn't actively attack humans due to its dragon-like nature, it has a very strong sense of territory, and it's not uncommon for it to attack intruders without question.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Bite (Head)","accuracy":"15 (22)","damage":"2d+14","evasion":"15 (22)","defense":12,"hp":{"value":112,"max":112},"mp":{"value":68,"max":68}},{"style":"Trample (Body)","accuracy":"16 (23)","damage":"2d+18","evasion":"13 (20)","defense":16,"hp":{"value":134,"max":134},"mp":{"value":45,"max":45}},{"style":"Tail (Tail)","accuracy":"15 (22)","damage":"2d+16","evasion":"14 (21)","defense":10,"hp":{"value":98,"max":98},"mp":{"value":36,"max":36}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"All Sections","description":""},{"title":"◯Underwater Aptitude","description":"There are no restrictions or penalties for actions in water."},{"title":"◯Poison, Disease Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯Delicate Loot","description":"If the HP of the Head section falls to 0 or less and the HP of the Body section is 1 or more, the loot of the &quot;Large Spike Shell&quot; will be lost."},{"title":"Head","description":""},{"title":"►Corrupting Breath / 15 (22) / Fortitude / Half","description":"Attack by exhaling a Corrupting Breath. Deals 2d+9 points of magic damage to &quot;Target: 1 area (4m radius)/10&quot; targets within &quot;Range: 1 (10m)&quot;. For 10 seconds (1 round), the target cannot perform actions involving vocalization, including casting spells, and cannot use Techniques. Effects already in place are not dispelled.\nThis effect is treated as Poison type."},{"title":"Body","description":""},{"title":"◯Hard Shell","description":"Does not receive critical hits from edged weapons, and is treated as having 3 higher Defense points against edged weapons."},{"title":"◯Shell Spikes","description":"When a target deals 1 or more points of applied damage to the Body section with a melee attack, &quot;Range: Touch&quot; effect, or similar effect, they immediately receive fixed damage equal to one-fifth of the applied damage (rounded up)."},{"title":"◯Left and Right Stomping","description":"Performs Trample twice with three pairs of left and right feet. The targets must be two different characters."},{"title":"⏩Defensive Stance","description":"Retracts the head and tail into the shell, taking a protective posture. Head and Tail sections cannot be targeted by Melee Attack, Ranged Attack, or effects with &quot;Target: 1 Character&quot;.\nThis effect can be used even if the Major Action of each retracted section has been completed. However, while retracted, each section cannot perform Major Actions or Minor Actions. Additionally, the retracted state is automatically released at the start of Tarrasque's turn after 10 seconds (1 round) of being retracted.\nThis ability can only be used once per round and cannot be used on consecutive turns."},{"title":"Tail","description":""},{"title":"◯Pervasive Rot / Can't","description":"Tail constantly diffuses rot poison from its base and between scales. All characters within Tail section and &quot;Range: Touch&quot; distance suffer a -2 penalty to Fortitude and Willpower checks against poison, disease effects. If Tail section is stored inside the Body section with [⏩Defensive Stance], the penalty is reduced to -1."},{"title":"🗨Tail Sweep","description":"Attacks up to 5 targets of choice within the skirmish area where it is present using the Tail. This ability cannot be used in consecutive turns."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Large Spike Shell (4,400G/Red S)"},{"roll":"2 - 6","loot":"Broken Spike (300G / Red A) x 1d"},{"roll":"7 - 12","loot":"Broken Spike (300G / Red A) x 2d"},{"roll":"13+","loot":"Hard Spike (1,440G / Red A) x 1d"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Tarrasque","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"dWrqM254X9KwOppi","name":"Bayard","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:bayard","level":9,"monsterType":"Mythical Beast","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Five senses","disposition":"Neutral","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Grasslands","reputation":16,"weakness":20,"weakPoint":"Water/Ice damage +3 points","initiative":19,"movementSpeed":"40 (4 Legs)","fortitude":"13 (20)","willpower":"11 (18)","source":"Natural History of Ursyla p. 134","description":"The Bayard is a rare horse-like Mythical Beast found in the grasslands of the Eyutorgo Mounted Nation, known as the &quot;Spirit Horse.&quot;\n\nThrough its somewhat translucent red body, one can see a golden heart beating. Its mane blazes with colors reminiscent of dancing flames.\n\nIts legs are terrifyingly swift, making it nearly impossible to catch up to. It possesses both a powerful physique and endurance and has the ability to achieve complete invisibility, vanishing from sight.\n\nThe Bayard may choose to serve those who defeat it. In the Eyutorgo Mounted Nation, there was a tradition where subduing a Bayard and making it one's personal mount was considered a great honor. Legend has it that it could increase its size to accommodate the number of riders.\n\nToday, their numbers are extremely scarce, making even encountering one difficult before any attempt at capture. Furthermore, in most cases, when a Bayard is defeated and dies, it causes its body to vanish completely.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Hooves","accuracy":"12 (19)","damage":"2d+14","evasion":"12 (19)","defense":9,"hp":{"value":84,"max":84},"mp":{"value":26,"max":26}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"⏩△Techniques","description":"They may use the [ Cat's Eyes ], [ Gazelle Feet ], [ Scale Leggings ], and [ Beetleskin ] Techniques."},{"title":"►Translucent","description":"Using this effect consumes 5 MP. For 10 minutes (60 rounds), they become Invisible (see CR II, p. 69) to characters with &quot;Perception: Five senses&quot; and &quot;Perception: Machines&quot;. Characters with &quot;Perception: Magic&quot; can still detect their presence.\nFor the duration, if they perform a Full Move or Major Action, the effect automatically ends immediately afterward."},{"title":"◯Acknowledge as Master","description":"If this monster's HP is between -20 and -10 when defeated, it will acknowledge its defeater as its &quot;Master&quot; and become their Mount . At this time, it will revive with 1 HP. Otherwise, it disappears without leaving a corpse."}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Bayard","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"eR2TlRVkH0wIVHJv","name":"Cuelebre","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:cuelebre","level":5,"monsterType":"Mythical Beast","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hungry","soulscars":0,"languages":"Sylvan","habitat":"Forests, Waterside, Caves","reputation":13,"weakness":16,"weakPoint":"Fire damage +3 points","initiative":15,"movementSpeed":"20 (Crawling) / 25 (Flying)","fortitude":"7 (14)","willpower":"7 (14)","source":"Natural History of Ursyla p. 133","description":"The Cuelebre is a large serpent with bat-like membrane wings. It measures about 1-2 meters in length, with extremely hard scales characterized by white coloring with black spots.\n\nThey are known to inhabit forests and spring sources in the Fairy Kingdom Federation Avalf and the Sebrae Forest Republic, where they have been spotted living alongside fairies.\n\nThey typically have a gentle temperament and don't attack indiscriminately. However, when hungry, they become extremely short-tempered and hunt animals for food. These animals can include humans.\n\nThey can also wield Fairy Magic, preferring to use wind and water spirits to avoid harming the forest. Their hard scales are said to deflect even bullets, and the highest quality ones are used as materials for &quot;Solid Scale Processing&quot; (see Natural History of Ursyla , p. 39).","combatStyles":[{"style":"Bite","accuracy":"7 (14)","damage":"2d+7","evasion":"6 (13)","defense":6,"hp":{"value":42,"max":42},"mp":{"value":31,"max":31}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯Flight","description":"Gain a +1 bonus modifier to Accuracy and Evasion checks for melee attacks."},{"title":"► Fairy Magic 5 Level / Magic Power 7 (14)","description":"Available types are Earth, Water/Ice, Wind, and Light. Even if you are using contract patterns (see MA, p. 136), it does not change."},{"title":"◯🗨►Magic Aptitude","description":"They can use the Combat Feats [ Multi-Action ], [ Targeting ], and [ Wordbreak ]."},{"title":"◯Delicate Loot","description":""}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"8+","loot":"Hardened Scales (900G/Gold Red A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Cuelebre","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"fak1H6Ovjq7p9SBQ","name":"Great Varg","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:great-varg","level":10,"monsterType":"Mythical Beast","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Neutral","soulscars":0,"languages":"Vargian","habitat":"Forests, Plains, Hills","reputation":15,"weakness":21,"weakPoint":"Fire damage + 3 points","initiative":21,"movementSpeed":"20 (4 Legs)","fortitude":"15 (22)","willpower":"13 (20)","source":"Monstrous Lore p. 180","description":"This is one of the strongest Vargs , reaching over 2.5 meters in height. If in a herd, they act as leaders. As a mutual recognition of strength, they often carry the Dark Trolls on their backs.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Bite","accuracy":"16 (23)","damage":"2d+12","evasion":"11 (18)","defense":9,"hp":{"value":98,"max":98},"mp":{"value":32,"max":32}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Rage","description":"When another Varg (of any type) in the same skirmish is defeated, the Brutal Varg gains a cumulative +2 bonus to damage for 10 seconds (1 round).\nThe GM decides when a Varg is defeated (incapacitated or dead)."},{"title":"◯ Final Reprimand","description":"When its HP falls to 0 or below, it emits a cry that inspires and empowers surrounding Vargs. All Vargs (of any type) within &quot;Range: Caster&quot; and &quot;Target: All areas (30m radius)/All&quot; gain a +4 bonus to Accuracy checks and +4 to Damage until the end of their next turn.\nThis effect is not cumulative."},{"title":"🗨 Power Strike II","description":"A Great Varg can deal an additional +12 damage on their next attack. However, any Evasion Check made by them this turn receives a -2 penalty."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"2 - 5","loot":"Fine Mythical Beast Hide (300G/Red A)"},{"roll":"6 - 9","loot":"Beautiful Mythical Beast Hide (800G/Gold Red A)"},{"roll":"10+","loot":"Silver-white Mythical Beast Hide (3,600G/Gold Red S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Great Varg","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"i0CMs9bwczXM2pFu","name":"Gurangatch","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:gurangatch","level":11,"monsterType":"Mythical Beast","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Neutral","soulscars":0,"languages":"Sea Animal, Sylvan","habitat":"Sea, Riverside","reputation":18,"weakness":21,"weakPoint":"Earth damage + 3 points","initiative":18,"movementSpeed":"20(Crawling)/40(Swimming)","fortitude":"14 (21)","willpower":"13 (20)","source":"CR II p. 395","description":"This is a mythical beast inhabiting the sea and rivers, with the front half of its body as a crocodile and the back half as a fish.\n\nIt circulates in a large territory and attacks violently against those it perceives to be violating its territory. As a result, its territory is a place where there are few dangerous predators. It is often is called the guardian of marine life by fishermen and others who live in the sea. However, they are rarely seen. In some areas, a folk song says, &quot;They live hard and sleep at the bottom of the sea.&quot;\n\nFor the mount version of this creature, see Gurangatch .","combatStyles":[{"style":"Front Legs (Front)","accuracy":"14 (21)","damage":"2d+15","evasion":"13 (20)","defense":14,"hp":{"value":105,"max":105},"mp":{"value":66,"max":66}},{"style":"Tail (Back)","accuracy":"13 (20)","damage":"2d+12","evasion":"14 (21)","defense":10,"hp":{"value":92,"max":92},"mp":{"value":23,"max":23}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"All Sections","description":""},{"title":"◯ Underwater Aptitude","description":""},{"title":"Front","description":""},{"title":"► Twin Strike &amp; Double Attack","description":"It can make two Front Legs attacks each round, though each attack requires its own Accuracy check. They may choose to attack different characters with each attack."},{"title":"► Fairy Magic 10 Level / Magic Power 12 (19)","description":"It can use Water/Ice, Wind, Light, and Dark types."},{"title":"◯ 🗨 ► Magic Aptitude","description":"They can use the Combat Feats [ Multi-Action ], [ Targeting ], [ Metamagic/Targets ], and [ Wordbreak ].\n[ Multi-Action ] can be declared when the monster uses [ ► Twin Strike &amp; Double Attack], and it can cast the spell after the second Accuracy check. The monster instead can use [ ► Twin Strike &amp; Double Attack] after it casts the spell, but not after using [ ► Jaw Bite]."},{"title":"► Jaw Bite/13 (20)/Danger Sense/Negates","description":"It feints with its arms and attack by biting with its jaws.\nWithin &quot;Range: Touch&quot; deals with a &quot;Target: 1 Character&quot; 2d+25 physical damage.\nThis unique skill cannot be used in consecutive turns. Once a character becomes a target of this effect, they gain a +4 bonus on Danger Sense checks to resist this effect until the end of combat."},{"title":"Back","description":""},{"title":"◯ Furious Tail","description":"In response to the threat to its own life, it becomes furious.\nIf the current HP of Front is less than 70 points, the Tail damage is increased by +2 points; if it is less than 40 points, another +2 points (total +4 points); if it is less than 15 points, another +4 points (total +8 points)."},{"title":"🗨 All-Out Attack","description":"A Tail can deal an additional 8 damage on its next attack. However, any Evasion check made by this section this turn receives a -3 penalty as a risk."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"2 - 6","loot":"Clean Scales (200G/Red A)"},{"roll":"7 - 11","loot":"Green Scales (1,600G/Gold Red S)"},{"roll":"12+","loot":"Langgan Scales (6,800/Gold Red S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Gurangatch","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"jxBDMOd3Dlj6d9nK","name":"Myrmecoleon","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:myrmecoleon","level":4,"monsterType":"Mythical Beast","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Caves, Wilderness, Shallows","reputation":10,"weakness":15,"weakPoint":"Physical damage +2 points","initiative":12,"movementSpeed":"14 (6 Legs)","fortitude":"6(13)","willpower":"6(13)","source":"AB, p. 115","description":"A Mythical Beast with a lion's head on the body of an ant with purple exoskeleton over 1m in length. While it can be spotted outdoors, most sightings have been reported within a Shallow Abyss. It possesses the ability to command Purple Ants , and cases of them moving together are frequently observed.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Bite","accuracy":"6(13)","damage":"2d+5","evasion":"&#32;","defense":5,"hp":{"value":5,"max":5},"mp":{"value":32,"max":32}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯Ant Leadership","description":"Provides a +1 bonus to Accuracy and Evasion checks for all Purple Ants within its current skirmish area.\nWhen in a Shallow Abyss, also adds +1 to [►Formic Acid] Success Value.\nThis effect does not stack even if there are multiple Myrmecoleons."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Abyss Shard (200G/-)"},{"roll":"2 - 5","loot":"Beetle Shell (30G/Red B)"},{"roll":"6 - 10","loot":"Good Quality Shell (150G/Red A)"},{"roll":"11+","loot":"Superior Shell (750G/Red A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Myrmecoleon","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"ks5viseWfY2AOwMA","name":"Sirin","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:sirin","level":3,"monsterType":"Mythical Beast","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five Senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Neutral","soulscars":0,"languages":"Elven, Arcana","habitat":"Forests, Shallows","reputation":10,"weakness":14,"weakPoint":"Physical damage +2 points","initiative":11,"movementSpeed":"11/22 (Flying)","fortitude":"4 (11)","willpower":"5 (12)","source":"AB, p. 115","description":"A mythical beast with a beautiful Humanoid woman's head and an owl's body. Based on physical characteristics and behavior, it is considered a subspecies of Deela Harpy . However, unlike the gentle, book-loving Deela Harpy, the Sirin is known for being mischievous, using enchanting songs to bewitch Humanoids and Barbarous creatures and luring them into a Shallow Abyss. They can freely travel between the Shallow and the outside world, and find utmost enjoyment in watching people who suddenly find themselves in the Shallow, frantically running around in confusion.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Claws","accuracy":"4(11)","damage":"2d","evasion":"&#32;","defense":4,"hp":{"value":2,"max":2},"mp":{"value":32,"max":32}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯Hard to Detect / 10 / Danger Sense / Negates","description":"The monster lurks with a barely visible body, waiting for an opportunity. When enemies approach within 10m of this monster, failing a Danger Sense check with Target Number 10 results in being surprised.\nWithin a Shallow Abyss, detection becomes even more difficult, and the Danger Sense check Target Number becomes 12.\nWhen Sirin succeeds with this effect's ambush, it often chooses to quickly leave the area without fighting."},{"title":"►Song of Victory / 3 (10) / Willpower / Negates","description":"With &quot;Range/Area: 2 (20m) / Target &quot;, the Sirin plays an enchanting song to &quot;Target: 1 Character.&quot; The target will try to move towards the singer, seeking them out as if drawn in.\nSirin can sing and maintain this song while performing a Normal Move.\nThis effect is treated as Psychic (Weak) type."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"2 - 10","loot":"Beautiful Feathers (30G/Gold Red B)"},{"roll":"11+","loot":"Large Feathers (200G/Red A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Sirin","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"ls4V8oY53WurKurw","name":"Emerald Raccoon","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:emerald-raccoon","level":6,"monsterType":"Mythical Beast","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Friendly","soulscars":0,"languages":"Lycant, Sylvan","habitat":"Forest","reputation":12,"weakness":15,"weakPoint":"Earth damage + 3 points","initiative":13,"movementSpeed":"16 (4 Legs)","fortitude":"8 (15)","willpower":"9 (16)","source":"CR III p. 392","description":"This is a Mythical Beast with green body hair of about 2m in length, inhabiting the forested areas of the Alframe continent, and looks like a raccoon dog. It can communicate with the same level of intellect as humans. It has a mild-mannered character and is a mediator between multiple Animals and Mythical Beasts in the forest ecosystem.\n\nIf a Humanoid or a Barbarous is trespassing on the territory of the Animals in the forest, they may use their magical powers to solve the problem.\n\nFor the mount version of this creature, see Emerald Raccoon .","combatStyles":[{"style":"Arms","accuracy":"8 (15)","damage":"2d+8","evasion":"8 (15)","defense":6,"hp":{"value":52,"max":52},"mp":{"value":48,"max":48}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"► Fairy Magic 6 Level / Magic Power 9 (16)","description":"Can use Earth, Water/Ice, Wind, and Light types."},{"title":"◯ 🗨 Magic Aptitude [Prerequisite: Unique Skill Release]","description":"They can use the Combat Feats [ Targeting ] and [ Metamagic/Targets ]."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Green Hair (250G/Red A)"},{"roll":"2 - 9","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"10+","loot":"Clean Green Hair (750G/Red A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Emerald Raccoon","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"noJTo1ynuj2qlVXl","name":"Gevaudan","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:gevaudan","level":6,"monsterType":"Mythical Beast","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Five senses","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Mountains, Forests, Grasslands","reputation":12,"weakness":15,"weakPoint":"Bludgeoning damage +3 points","initiative":14,"movementSpeed":"25 (4 Legs)","fortitude":"8 (15)","willpower":"8 (15)","source":"Natural History of Dorden p. 130","description":"Gevaudan is a wolf-like Mythical Beast that inhabits the northern part of Dorden, around the Northern Fang Mountain range and the Fresian Forest Country. Although its body length exceeds 2m, its build itself gives a slender and supple impression. Compared to its body, the head is large, with an elongated snout and numerous jagged teeth. At first glance, its fur appears solid black, but it has a striped pattern of near-black gray and jet black. Its winding tail ends with a tuft and spikes similar to a lion's.\n\nIts nature is extremely ferocious, and it enjoys hunting by weakening its prey by sucking blood via the spikes on its tail before finishing them off. Due to this nature, some Gevaudans are known to accompany Vampires .\n\nThey particularly favor cow's blood; occasionally, individuals venture out from mountains and forests onto grasslands to hunt livestock. The people of Magnoa fear and despise them, referring to them as &quot;The Beast&quot;.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Bite (Head)","accuracy":"8 (15)","damage":"2d+8","evasion":"8 (15)","defense":5,"hp":{"value":51,"max":51},"mp":{"value":20,"max":20}},{"style":"Tail (Body)","accuracy":"7 (14)","damage":"2d+6","evasion":"7 (14)","defense":6,"hp":{"value":54,"max":54},"mp":{"value":14,"max":14}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"All Sections","description":""},{"title":"◯Normal Weapon Immunity","description":""},{"title":"Head","description":""},{"title":"►Terrifying Roar / 8 (15) / Willpower / Negates","description":"Gevaudan lets out a roar that instills fear in its opponents. Targets within a &quot;radius of 5m (1 area)/All&quot; centered on itself receive a -2 penalty to Accuracy and Evasion checks for 10 seconds (1 round).\nThis action cannot be performed in consecutive turns.\nThis effect is treated as Psychic type."},{"title":"⏩△Techniques","description":"They may use the [ Cat's Eyes ], [ Bear Muscle ], and [ Gazelle Feet ] Techniques."},{"title":"Body","description":""},{"title":"►Twin Strike &amp; Double Attack","description":"Gevaudan can make two Tail attacks each round. After checking the result of the first attack, the monster can choose whether to make a second attack on the same target further or on a different target of their choice."},{"title":"◯Blood-Sucking Spikes","description":"When a Tail attack hits and deals 1 or more points of applied damage, one section of Gevaudan's choice recovers 3 HP."},{"title":"◯Delicate Loot","description":"If the Body section HP drops to 0 or below, the &quot;Glittering Spikes&quot; loot is lost."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Glittering Spikes (750G/Red A)"},{"roll":"2 - 9","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"10+","loot":"Dark Grey Fur (300G/Red A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Gevaudan","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"oxtsLNjXQ2M25QuM","name":"Griffon","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:griffon","level":7,"monsterType":"Mythical Beast","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Five senses","disposition":"Neutral","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Mountains","reputation":12,"weakness":18,"weakPoint":"Wind type damage +3 points","initiative":18,"movementSpeed":"20 (4 Legs)/40 (Flying)","fortitude":"12 (19)","willpower":"9 (16)","source":"CR I p. 428","description":"A mythical beast with the head and wings of an eagle and the body of a lion. Griffons are surprisingly agile in the air for their bulk and often nest in holes dug into cliffsides. A Griffon is attracted to and tends to collect shining objects, such as precious metals and gemstones. If they find an intruder trying to steal their shinies, a Griffon will attack violently. Rarely some Griffons understand the Trade Common language.\n\nFor the mount version of this creature, see Griffon (mount) .","combatStyles":[{"style":"Beak (Body)","accuracy":"9 (16)","damage":"2d+11","evasion":"11 (18)","defense":5,"hp":{"value":58,"max":58},"mp":{"value":26,"max":26}},{"style":"Wing (Wing)","accuracy":"10 (17)","damage":"2d+8","evasion":"9 (16)","defense":4,"hp":{"value":39,"max":39},"mp":{"value":11,"max":11}},{"style":"Wing (Wing)","accuracy":"10 (17)","damage":"2d+8","evasion":"9 (16)","defense":4,"hp":{"value":39,"max":39},"mp":{"value":11,"max":11}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"All Sections","description":""},{"title":"◯ Continuous Attack","description":"If a Griffon successfully hits a target in melee, they may make a second attack against the same target."},{"title":"Wing","description":""},{"title":"◯ Flight","description":"A Griffon receives a +1 bonus to Accuracy and Evasion only for melee attacks.\nIf one of the Wings falls to 0 HP or lower, this unique skill cannot be used."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"2 - 5","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"6 - 12","loot":"Gems (150G/Gold A) x 1d"},{"roll":"13+","loot":"Mithril (2,600G/Gold S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Griffon","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"pgPLDIuA9fr6squg","name":"Abyssal Lesser Dragon","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:abyssal-lesser-dragon","level":14,"monsterType":"Mythical Beast","intelligence":"High","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"Trade Common, Dragonic, Daemonic, Arcana","habitat":"Caves","reputation":16,"weakness":21,"weakPoint":"Physical Damage +2 points","initiative":19,"movementSpeed":"15 / 30 (Flying)","fortitude":"18(25)","willpower":"18(25)","source":"AB, p. 120","description":"This is a dragon with ominous purple scales. It is a Lesser Dragon (see CR II, p. 396 or ML, p. 182) that has been transformed by absorbing the power of the Shallow Abyss, and under the Shallow's influence, it is possessed by destructive impulses. It has an instinct to collect large amounts of Abyss Shards, which are said to be piled high in its lair.\n\nWhile this data describes a Lesser Dragon that has become an Abyss Dragon, other dragon classes would possess corresponding powers when transformed. These are also expected to be extremely dangerous, with increased violence and impulsivity due to a Shallow's influence.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Bite (Head)","accuracy":"18(25)","damage":"2d+20","evasion":"&#32;","defense":16,"hp":{"value":17,"max":17},"mp":{"value":32,"max":32}},{"style":"Tail (Body)","accuracy":"17(24)","damage":"2d+18","evasion":"&#32;","defense":14,"hp":{"value":19,"max":19},"mp":{"value":32,"max":32}},{"style":"Wing (Wing)","accuracy":"16(23)","damage":"2d+16","evasion":"&#32;","defense":14,"hp":{"value":16,"max":16},"mp":{"value":32,"max":32}},{"style":"Wing (Wing)","accuracy":"16(23)","damage":"2d+16","evasion":"&#32;","defense":14,"hp":{"value":16,"max":16},"mp":{"value":32,"max":32}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"All Sections","description":""},{"title":"◯Fire Immunity, ◯Curse Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯Shallow Aptitude","description":"Within a Shallow Abyss, all sections receive a +1 bonus to all skill check results."},{"title":"Head","description":""},{"title":"► Truespeech Magic , Spiritualism Magic , Abyssal Magic 11 Level / Magic Power 15 (22)","description":"When using Abyssal Magic, enhancement effects can be used up to 3 rounds."},{"title":"◯🗨►Magic Aptitude","description":"They can use Combat Feats [ Targeting ], [ Magic Convergence ], [ Magic Control ], [ Universal Metamagic ], and [ Wordbreak ]."},{"title":"►Magic Fire Breath / 16 (23) / Fortitude / Half","description":"With &quot;Range/Area: 2 (20m) / Shot &quot;, breathes fire at &quot;Target: 1 area (6m radius) / 20&quot;, dealing 2d+20 points of Fire- and Curse-type magic damage.\nThis ability cannot be used in consecutive turns."},{"title":"Body","description":""},{"title":"🗨Tail Sweep","description":"Chooses up to 5 characters capable of melee attacks and performs a Tail attack against them.\nThis ability cannot be used in consecutive turns."},{"title":"◯Attack Obstacle = Impossible • None","description":"Its size hinders attack.\nThe Head section cannot be attacked with Melee Attacks.\nWhen the Body section falls to 0 HP or lower, this effect disappears."},{"title":"Wing","description":""},{"title":"🗨 All-Out Attack","description":"A Wing can deal an additional 8 damage on its next attack. However, any Evasion check made by this section this turn receives a -3 penalty as a risk."},{"title":"◯Flight","description":"An Abyssal Lesser Dragon receives a +1 bonus to Accuracy and Evasion only for melee attacks. If any Wings fall to 0 HP or lower, this unique skill cannot be used."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Abyss Shard (200G/-) x 2d"},{"roll":"2 - 5","loot":"Dragon Fang (1,200G/Red S)"},{"roll":"6 - 11","loot":"Dragon Scale (5,000G/Red S)"},{"roll":"12+","loot":"Dragon Jewel (10,000G/Gold SS)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Abyssal Lesser Dragon","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"r71wThv2VdpdCoU5","name":"Petsuchos","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:petsuchos","level":9,"monsterType":"Mythical Beast","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Neutral","soulscars":0,"languages":"Elven, Sylvan","habitat":"Rivers, Lakes","reputation":15,"weakness":21,"weakPoint":"Fire damage +3 points","initiative":14,"movementSpeed":"13 (4 Legs) / 20 (Swimming)","fortitude":"12 (19)","willpower":"12 (19)","source":"BM","description":"This is a mythical beast in the shape of a giant 7-meter-long crocodile with pure white scales.\n\nDespite their fearsome appearance, they are gentle and thoughtful and are self-appointed guardians of great rivers and lakes. Together, they will attack without mercy anyone who harms those who live in the water or who destroy the watery places.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Jaw (Body)","accuracy":"11 (18)","damage":"2d+13","evasion":"10 (17)","defense":11,"hp":{"value":91,"max":91},"mp":{"value":53,"max":53}},{"style":"Tail (Tail)","accuracy":"11 (18)","damage":"2d+11","evasion":"10 (17)","defense":10,"hp":{"value":76,"max":76},"mp":{"value":33,"max":33}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"All Sections","description":""},{"title":"◯ Underwater Aptitude","description":""},{"title":"Body","description":""},{"title":"► Fairy Magic 9 Level / Magic Power 11 (18)","description":"Can cast Water/Ice type up to 9 ranks. This does not change even if the contract pattern is adopted (see MA, p. 136)."},{"title":"◯ 🗨 ► Magic Aptitude","description":"They can use the Combat Feats [ Multi-Action ], [ Targeting ], [ Magic Convergence ], [ Magic Control ], [ Hawk Eye ], [ Universal Metamagic ], and [ Wordbreak ]."},{"title":"Tail","description":""},{"title":"🗨 Tail Swing II","description":"A Tail attack hits up to 5 targets in the skirmish Petsuchos is in."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"2 - 5","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"6 - 7","loot":"Crocodile Skin (200G/Red A)"},{"roll":"8 - 9","loot":"Superior Crocodile Skin (600G/Red A)"},{"roll":"10+","loot":"Pure White Crocodile Skin (1,800G/Red S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Petsuchos","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"ruRx3upQ1zzqT70p","name":"Jii","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:jii","level":7,"monsterType":"Mythical Beast","intelligence":"High","perception":"Five senses","disposition":"Neutral","soulscars":0,"languages":"Trade common, Sylvan","habitat":"Unknown","reputation":14,"weakness":18,"weakPoint":"Accuracy +1","initiative":17,"movementSpeed":"12 (4 Legs)/-","fortitude":"9 (16)","willpower":"11 (18)","source":"BM","description":"The Jii is a creature with the body of a cow and a human face. It has well- developed hind legs that allow it to walk on two legs. According to tradition, the Jii appears before major disasters and utters prophecies. In some nations, the mere appearance of the Jii is considered a sign of an impending disaster.\n\nAlthough typically kind and hospitable, the Jii can become aggressive towards those with malicious intentions. The origin of the Jii is unknown, but sightings have been reported in deep forests and on high mountain peaks.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Hoof","accuracy":"7 (14)","damage":"2d+6","evasion":"8 (15)","defense":6,"hp":{"value":64,"max":64},"mp":{"value":70,"max":70}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"► Divine Magic , Fairy Magic 7 Level / Magic Power 11 (18)","description":"Can use Earth, Wind, Dark, and Light types.\nIf a contract pattern is adopted (see MA, p. 136), it knows all types (5 ranks, special 2 ranks)."},{"title":"◯ 🗨 ► Magic Aptitude","description":"They can use the Combat Feats [ Targeting ], [ Metamagic/Accuracy ], and [ Wordbreak ]."},{"title":"🗨 Foresight","description":"This ability can be declared only before the Major Action.\nFor 10 seconds (1 round) Jii gains a +2 bonus to Evasion checks. At the same time, it receives a -2 penalty to its Accuracy check."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"2 - 6","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"7+","loot":"Sharp Hoof (950G/Red A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Jii","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"t8nHLmRXz6j8q0pD","name":"Unicorn","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:unicorn","level":6,"monsterType":"Mythical Beast","intelligence":"High","perception":"Five senses","disposition":"Neutral","soulscars":0,"languages":"Sylvan","habitat":"Forest","reputation":10,"weakness":15,"weakPoint":"Accuracy +1","initiative":14,"movementSpeed":"20 (4 Legs)","fortitude":"10 (17)","willpower":"10 (17)","source":"CR II p. 391","description":"Unicorns are elegant creatures, horse-like, with long, iridescent spiraling horns on their forehead. They are intelligent but very skittish, only appearing to human maidens and even then, quite rarely.\n\nThey are hunted by both outlaws and Barbarous for their horn, which can cure diseases and heal wounds even after it is removed from the Unicorn.\n\nThe horn has the entirety of the Unicorn's MP stored in it, and when cut it retains the Unicorn's current MP (killing the Unicorn in the process) and can be used as a Unicorn Horn .","combatStyles":[{"style":"Horn","accuracy":"8 (15)","damage":"2d+6","evasion":"7 (14)","defense":5,"hp":{"value":50,"max":50},"mp":{"value":80,"max":80}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"► Fairy Magic 6 Level/Magic Power 8 (15)","description":"Can use Earth, Water/Ice, Light, and Dark types."},{"title":"◯ 🗨 Magic Aptitude","description":"They can use the Combat Feats [ Targeting ], [ Magic Convergence ], [ Magic Control ], [ Hawk Eye ], and [ Metamagic/Targets ]."},{"title":"► Healing Horn/10 (17)/Fortitude/Negates","description":"It touches the &quot;Target: 1 Character&quot; with a horn to heal the target's HP by 50 points. If the Fortitude check was the favorable result in the success value comparison, the target will also be completely cured of any poison, disease, curse, petrification, etc. that it has been subjected to. It is also possible to apply this effect to itself.\nHowever, this effect does not apply to Constructs and Magitech characters. Furthermore, if the character touched by the horn is Undead, not only is it immune to the aforementioned effects, but it must also perform a Fortitude and, if it fails, suffer magic damage of 50 points.\nA character can only receive this effect once per day. In the case of a character with multiple sections, each section can be affected up to once per day.\nUsing this unique skill consumes 10 points of MP."},{"title":"◯ Horn of Mana","description":"If the Unicorn's MP reaches 0, it dies instantly, its horn crumbling into useless dust."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Unicorn Horn (Remaining MP x 300G/Gold Red A â SS)"},{"roll":"2+","loot":"Nothing"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Unicorn","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"tF2hqddhEmJPPevD","name":"Kamawet","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:kamawet","level":4,"monsterType":"Mythical Beast","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five senses","disposition":"Friendly","soulscars":0,"languages":"Dragonic","habitat":"Sea","reputation":5,"weakness":12,"weakPoint":"Lightning damage + 3 points","initiative":10,"movementSpeed":"5(Crawling)/30(Swimming)","fortitude":"7 (14)","willpower":"6 (13)","source":"Monstrous Lore p. 174","description":"Kamawets are sea-based mythical beasts, similar in appearance to a dragon without wings. Only a few meters long, they are mild-mannered and rather friendly, and are able to coexist with Humanoids quite easily. Subsisting on a mostly fish diet, they rarely travel outside of the water. Sometimes, it even can carry humanoids on its back.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Slam","accuracy":"5 (12)","damage":"2d+4","evasion":"5 (12)","defense":3,"hp":{"value":33,"max":33},"mp":{"value":16,"max":16}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Underwater Specialization","description":"Can move in water without penalties and restrictions. Conversely, all action checks are subject to a -2 penalty on the ground."},{"title":"◯ Water/Ice Immunity","description":""}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"2 - 6","loot":"Chipped Fangs (100G/Red A)"},{"roll":"7+","loot":"Kamawet Fangs (500G/Red A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Kamawet","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"tb5264bdvAPjZ7x3","name":"Black Griffon","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:black-griffon","level":9,"monsterType":"Mythical Beast","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five senses","disposition":"Neutral","soulscars":0,"languages":"Trade Common, Barbaric","habitat":"Mountains","reputation":15,"weakness":20,"weakPoint":"Wind-type Damage +3 points","initiative":20,"movementSpeed":"20 (4 Legs)/40 (Flying)","fortitude":"14 (21)","willpower":"11 (18)","source":"Natural History of Burlight p. 131","description":"This is a subspecies of Griffon with a larger body than usual, covered with black feathers. It exhibits strong territorial behavior and perceives flying intruders as either prey or threats, behaving aggressively towards them. They do not share territory with other Griffons except during mating or when raising young. While it is possible for them to breed with common Griffon species, the offspring resulting from such unions have not been studied yet.\n\nThey are marginally more tolerant of ground intruders. They possess the ability to understand and communicate using language, although their speech may be somewhat difficult to comprehend. If they perceive themselves to have a significant advantage, they can engage in negotiations. However, they generally display arrogance and react quickly to provocative words and actions, so caution should be exercised in one's choice of words and attitude if attempting to negotiate with them.\n\nThere is a theory that they call thunder because they prey on Thunderbirds . Regardless of the veracity of this theory, the Electric Feather obtained from them is useful as a material for creating the accessory &quot;Thunder Feather&quot; (see Natural History of Burlight p. 43).","combatStyles":[{"style":"Beak (Body)","accuracy":"12 (19)","damage":"2d+14","evasion":"13 (20)","defense":8,"hp":{"value":83,"max":83},"mp":{"value":36,"max":36}},{"style":"Wing (Wing)","accuracy":"13 (20)","damage":"2d+10","evasion":"12 (19)","defense":6,"hp":{"value":69,"max":69},"mp":{"value":21,"max":21}},{"style":"Wing (Wing)","accuracy":"13 (20)","damage":"2d+10","evasion":"12 (19)","defense":6,"hp":{"value":69,"max":69},"mp":{"value":21,"max":21}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"All Sections","description":""},{"title":"◯Lightning Resistance","description":"Automatically reduces the amount of Lightning type damage it takes by -3 points."},{"title":"◯Delicate Loot","description":"The loot &quot;Electric Feather&quot; will be given for each time any section of the Black Griffon is damaged by Lightning-type attacks (including when applied damage is 0 or caused by its own [⏩Heavy Thunder]) during the battle. The total number of Electric Feathers cannot exceed 10."},{"title":"Body","description":""},{"title":"⏩△Techniques","description":"They may use the [ Cat's Eyes ], [ Beetleskin ], [ Bear Muscle ], and [ Recovery (9 pts.) ] Techniques."},{"title":"◯Continuous Attack II","description":"If the Body successfully hits a target in melee, they may make a second attack. They can make a third attack against the same target if a second attack hits."},{"title":"⏩Heavy Thunder / 11 (18) / Willpower / Half","description":"Once per turn within &quot;Range: Caster,&quot; the Black Griffon causes a single lightning strike on &quot;Target: All Areas (30m Radius)/Space.&quot; It selects 1 character randomly from all characters (including its own 3 sections) in the area and deals &quot;2d+10&quot; Lightning magic damage to it.\nThe same character (section) cannot be hit by this effect more than once in the same turn."},{"title":"Wings","description":""},{"title":"◯Continuous Attack","description":"If a Wing successfully hits a target in melee, it may make a second attack against the same target."},{"title":"◯ Flight","description":"All sections receive a +1 bonus to Accuracy and Evasion only for melee attacks.\nIf one of the Wings falls to 0 HP or lower, this unique skill cannot be used."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Electric Feather (200G/Gold Red A)"},{"roll":"2 - 6","loot":"Black Feathers (80G/Red B)"},{"roll":"7 - 9","loot":"Black Shiny Feathers (300G/Red A)"},{"roll":"10+","loot":"Obsidian Feathers (1,200G/Red S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Black Griffon","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"tvDNVcnlCY2SRIKB","name":"Achlis","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:achlis","level":2,"monsterType":"Mythical Beast","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Five senses","disposition":"Neutral","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Meadows","reputation":9,"weakness":12,"weakPoint":"Physical damage +2 points","initiative":9,"movementSpeed":"12 (4 Legs)","fortitude":"4 (11)","willpower":"3 (10)","source":"VC","description":"This Mythical Beast is about 2 meters long, with white fur and a llama- like appearance. It is characterized by small horns sprouting from both of its foreheads and jointless hind legs. The creature is highly sensitive and can become aggressive when influenced by the emotions and intentions of others.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Bite (Front)","accuracy":"4 (11)","damage":"2d+1","evasion":"4 (11)","defense":3,"hp":{"value":18,"max":18},"mp":{"value":10,"max":10}},{"style":"Kick (Rear)","accuracy":"4 (11)","damage":"2d+4","evasion":"3 (10)","defense":4,"hp":{"value":14,"max":14},"mp":{"value":6,"max":6}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"Front","description":""},{"title":"⏩ Intimidating Cry / 3 (10) / Fortitude / Negates","description":"The Achlis makes an intimidating cry and causes enemies around it to panic. Within &quot;Range: Caster&quot; and &quot;Target: 1 area (3m Radius)/All,&quot; targets suffer a -1 penalty on Accuracy, and Evasion checks for 10 seconds (1 round).\nThis effect can be used only once per round and cannot be used in consecutive turns."},{"title":"Rear","description":""},{"title":"◯ Standing Upright","description":"If the HP of the Rear is 0 or less, Front section gets a -2 penalty on Evasion checks."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"2 - 6","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"7 - 10","loot":"White Fur (60G/Red A)"},{"roll":"11+","loot":"Pure White Fur (130G/Red A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Achlis","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"uIBQqnBFqLiFYGBZ","name":"Deela Harpy","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:deela-harpy","level":3,"monsterType":"Mythical Beast","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Neutral","soulscars":0,"languages":"Elven, Arcana","habitat":"Forests, Mountain","reputation":8,"weakness":14,"weakPoint":"Physical damage +2 points","initiative":11,"movementSpeed":"13/26(Flying)","fortitude":"5 (12)","willpower":"5 (12)","source":"CR I p. 426","description":"A mythical beast, combining the appearance of a bird with that of a beautiful woman. Quietly interacting with Humans since the Magic Civilization period, Deela Harpy now lives deep in mountains and forests. If one happens to know either the Arcana or Elven languages, it is quite possible to converse with Deela Harpy.\n\nOften mild-mannered, a Deela Harpy avoids fights with Humanoids unless there is a compelling reason to do so. In addition, some prefer reading to talking, and some carry manuscripts of books dating back to the Magic Civilization period.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Claws","accuracy":"4 (11)","damage":"2d","evasion":"5 (12)","defense":2,"hp":{"value":24,"max":24},"mp":{"value":21,"max":21}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"► Enchanting Song / 3 (10) / Willpower / Negates","description":"Deela Harpy sings a song with &quot;Range/Area: 2 (20m) / Target &quot; to &quot;Target: 1 Character&quot;. The target obeys Deela Harpy's commands in the song's lyrics.\nThe commands must be in a language that the target understands. The commands must be simple, and the target will not obey any commands to harm themselves.\nThis effect is treated as Psychic (Weak) type."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"2 - 9","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"10+","loot":"Arcana-Language Book (170G/White A) x 1d"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Deela Harpy","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"uawFRBLYEbfCQqk6","name":"Ypotryll","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:ypotryll","level":8,"monsterType":"Mythical Beast","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Shallows","reputation":15,"weakness":18,"weakPoint":"Fire damage +3 points","initiative":16,"movementSpeed":"20 (4 Legs)","fortitude":"11 (18)","willpower":"10 (17)","source":"AB, p. 117","description":"Ypotryll is a mythical beast about 5 meters long with a boar's head, camel's hump, goat's legs, and a long snake-like tail. It has an extremely cruel nature, preferring to impale its prey with its long fangs and torment them for sport.\n\nFor some reason, this monster is only seen within Shallow Abysses, leading some to believe that, combined with its hideously grotesque appearance, it might be the manifestation of nightmares from those who were once trapped in the Shallow.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Bite (Head)","accuracy":"11(18)","damage":"2d+11","evasion":"&#32;","defense":10,"hp":{"value":7,"max":7},"mp":{"value":32,"max":32}},{"style":"Stomp (Body)","accuracy":"10(17)","damage":"2d+11","evasion":"&#32;","defense":10,"hp":{"value":7,"max":7},"mp":{"value":32,"max":32}},{"style":"Tail (Tail)","accuracy":"11(18)","damage":"2d+10","evasion":"&#32;","defense":9,"hp":{"value":6,"max":6},"mp":{"value":32,"max":32}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"All Sections","description":""},{"title":"►Charge / 11 (18) / Evasion / Negates","description":"With &quot;Range/Area: 1 (60m) / Breakthrough &quot;, the Ypotryll runs through and deals 2d+11 points of physical damage to the target, then knocks them prone.\nTo use this ability, it must be able to perform a Full Move, all sections must be able to act, and it must be used before taking a Major Action with any section. After using this ability, all sections end their Major Action and receive a -4 penalty to Evasion checks for the next 10 seconds (1 round)."},{"title":"Head","description":""},{"title":"🗨Uppercut","description":"Can only be declared when the target has only one section, is bipedal, and is standing directly on the ground with both feet only. When the Bite attack hits, it deals damage and simultaneously knocks the target prone."},{"title":"Body","description":""},{"title":"►Double Attack (Stomp)","description":"This effect can only be used on prone characters. Perform consecutive Stomps. Executes two consecutive Stomp attacks."},{"title":"◯Attack Obstacle = +4 ・ None","description":"Size hinders the attack.\nHead section gain a +4 bonus to Evasion checks against melee attacks.\nWhen Body section's HP drops to 0 or below, this effect is lost."},{"title":"Tail","description":""},{"title":"◯Long Tail","description":"Can make melee attacks with Tail within &quot;Range/Area: 2 (20m) / Target .&quot;"},{"title":"🗨Tail Sweep","description":"Choose up to 5 characters that can be targeted by melee attacks (including those enabled by [◯Long Tail]) and perform Tail attacks against them.\nThis ability cannot be used in consecutive turns."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Abyss Shard (200G/-)"},{"roll":"2 - 8","loot":"Curved Fangs (200G/Red A)"},{"roll":"9 - 11","loot":"Long and Sharp Fangs (800G/Red A)"},{"roll":"12+","loot":"Ferocious Long Fangs (3,200G/Red S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Ypotryll","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"wHBLy9wvfE9mvczd","name":"Catoblepas","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:catoblepas","level":9,"monsterType":"Mythical Beast","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Lakes, Swamps","reputation":17,"weakness":20,"weakPoint":"Fire damage + 3 points","initiative":16,"movementSpeed":"15 (4 Legs)/15(Swimming)","fortitude":"12 (19)","willpower":"12 (19)","source":"Monstrous Lore p. 179","description":"A Catoblepas is a mythical beast about 3 meters long with the head of a pig and the body of a buffalo. Its eyes are iridescent and shiny, and it petrifies people by looking at them, regardless of their intentions. It can sense its surroundings even while blinded, so it usually lives with its eyes closed.\n\nSelf-righteous and solitary, it regards anyone who approaches them as an enemy. Its skin has power that repels evil, and in rare cases, the effect remains even after death and can be sold for a high price.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Hooves","accuracy":"12 (19)","damage":"2d+14","evasion":"11 (18)","defense":10,"hp":{"value":82,"max":82},"mp":{"value":41,"max":41}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Lightning Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Curse Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Underwater Aptitude","description":""},{"title":"⏩ Petrified Hooves/12 (19)/Willpower/Negates","description":"Catoblepas stares at 1 character with &quot;Range/Area: 2 (50m) / Target &quot;. On failed save target is petrified (Dexterity, Agility/-6) (see ML p. 71).\nThis effect is treated as a Curse type.\nThis unique skill can be used up to twice per round, but targets must be different."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Petrifying Hooves (1,200G/Gold Red Black S) x 2"},{"roll":"2 - 9","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"10+","loot":"Slimy Skin (680G/Red A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Catoblepas","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"xRxsuQbPRjjJUFLK","name":"Monoceros","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:monoceros","level":8,"monsterType":"Mythical Beast","intelligence":"High","perception":"Five senses","disposition":"Neutral","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Forests, Grasslands","reputation":16,"weakness":19,"weakPoint":"Physical damage +2 points","initiative":15,"movementSpeed":"23 (4 Legs)/-","fortitude":"11 (18)","willpower":"10 (17)","source":"BM","description":"The Monocerous is a holy bull. The horns on his forehead enhance its Magic Power, allowing it to perform powerful magic. It is highly intelligent, but it does not speak.\n\nIt is calm and quiet but can defend itself. It is especially unrelenting when it comes to those who offend its pride.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Horn (Front)","accuracy":"10 (17)","damage":"2d+12","evasion":"10 (17)","defense":6,"hp":{"value":69,"max":69},"mp":{"value":62,"max":62}},{"style":"Hoof (Rear)","accuracy":"11 (18)","damage":"2d+10","evasion":"9 (16)","defense":8,"hp":{"value":81,"max":81},"mp":{"value":36,"max":36}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"Front","description":""},{"title":"► Truespeech Magic , Divine Magic 8 Level / Magic Power 11 (18)","description":""},{"title":"◯ 🗨 Magic Aptitude","description":"They can use the Combat Feats [ Targeting ], [ Hawk Eye ], and [ Metamagic/Targets ]."},{"title":"⏩ Powerful Magic","description":"Monoceros fills an area with mana and enhances Magic Power, gaining a +2 bonus to the Spellcasting checks for one round (10 seconds). This effect is not cumulative and using this unique skill costs 10 MP."},{"title":"Rear","description":""},{"title":"⏩ △ Techniques","description":"They may use the [ Bear Muscle ], [ Beetleskin ], and [ Recovery (5 pts.) ] Techniques."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Monoceros Horn (1,300G/Red S)"},{"roll":"2 - 7","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"8+","loot":"Sharp Hoof (950G/Red A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Monoceros","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"xk7BgbkWVaVQ9Gp5","name":"Wyvern","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:wyvern","level":7,"monsterType":"Mythical Beast","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Five senses","disposition":"Hungry","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Mountains","reputation":8,"weakness":15,"weakPoint":"Accuracy +1","initiative":16,"movementSpeed":"15/30 (Flying)","fortitude":"9 (16)","willpower":"8 (15)","source":"CR III (2.0) p. 374","description":"Wyverns are an offshoot of dragons, similar in appearance, though their wings have taken the place of their forelimbs. These particular Wyverns are covered in fine black scales that glitter with a dark luster while the Wyvern is in motion. Fully outstretched, the bat-like wings average a span of around 10m, giving the Wyvern a fearsome appearance even in the dark. It is the patagium, or membrane, of these wings that are highly coveted, as they are used as the basis for a number of premium leather products.\n\nSky Wyverns are a smaller subspecies of this monster.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Bite (Head)","accuracy":"11 (18)","damage":"2d+9","evasion":"10 (17)","defense":7,"hp":{"value":38,"max":38},"mp":{"value":31,"max":31}},{"style":"Talon (Wing)","accuracy":"10 (17)","damage":"2d+7","evasion":"9 (16)","defense":5,"hp":{"value":29,"max":29},"mp":{"value":29,"max":29}},{"style":"Talon (Wing)","accuracy":"10 (17)","damage":"2d+7","evasion":"9 (16)","defense":5,"hp":{"value":29,"max":29},"mp":{"value":29,"max":29}},{"style":"Tail (Tail)","accuracy":"10 (17)","damage":"2d+6","evasion":"8 (15)","defense":6,"hp":{"value":33,"max":33},"mp":{"value":26,"max":26}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"All Sections","description":""},{"title":"⏩ △ Techniques","description":"They may use the [ Beetleskin ], [ Cat's Eyes ], and [ Recovery (5 points) ] Techniques."},{"title":"Head","description":""},{"title":"► Fire Breath/10 (17)/Fortitude/Half","description":"With &quot;Range/Area: 2 (20m)/ Shot &quot;, spits fire at &quot;Target: 1 area (3m Radius) / 5&quot;, dealing 2d+10 Fire magic damage."},{"title":"Wing","description":""},{"title":"◯ Flight","description":"A Wyvern receives a +1 bonus to Accuracy and Evasion only for melee attacks. If any Wings fall to 0 HP or lower, this unique skill cannot be used."},{"title":"Tail","description":""},{"title":"🗨 Tail Sweep","description":"The monster can use its tail to attack up to 5 targets in the same skirmish. An Accuracy check is made on all characters at once, and damage is determined individually.\nThis attack cannot be used in consecutive rounds."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"2 - 6","loot":"Draconic Patagium (1,000G/Red S)"},{"roll":"7 - 12","loot":"Black Dragon Patagium (1,000G/Red S)"},{"roll":"13+","loot":"Lustrous Black Dragon Patagium (5,000G/Gold Red S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Wyvern","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"yA3TtvHQro92Z6k3","name":"Charm Bear","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:charm-bear","level":5,"monsterType":"Mythical Beast","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Neutral","soulscars":0,"languages":"Lycant, Sylvan","habitat":"Forests","reputation":13,"weakness":16,"weakPoint":"Water/Ice damage +3 points","initiative":13,"movementSpeed":"18 (4 Legs)","fortitude":"7 (14)","willpower":"7 (14)","source":"Natural History of Burlight p. 131","description":"Charm Bears are Mythical Beasts that reside in the forests of the Burlight Region. They are small in size, resembling bear cubs, and are covered in bright brown fur.\n\nDespite their charming appearance and gestures, they are mischievous creatures who have no qualms about lying and cheating. Their conversations consist of a mixture of truth and lies, making it challenging to determine what to believe.\n\nCharm Bears are friendly and talkative, and enjoy engaging in pleasant conversations. However, they have a tendency to do the opposite of what they are asked or to act based on vague wishes they sense from others.\n\nDespite their mischievous nature, they do not physically harm others and try to avoid causing direct harm to life and health. They rarely engage in fights and prioritize fleeing over confrontation.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Bite","accuracy":"7 (14)","damage":"2d+7","evasion":"7 (14)","defense":5,"hp":{"value":42,"max":42},"mp":{"value":42,"max":42}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"►Magic (1 System) 5 Level / Magic Power 7 (14)","description":"Can cast Fairy Magic or Nature Magic up to the 5th level, and the types used when learning Fairy Magic are Earth, Wind, Light, and Dark. Even if you are using contract patterns (see MA, p. 136), it does not change."},{"title":"◯🗨►Magic Aptitude","description":"They can use the Combat Feats [ Multi-Action ], [ Targeting ], [ Hawk Eye ], [ Universal Metamagic ], and [ Wordbreak ]."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"2 - 5","loot":"Mythical Beast Hide (140G/Red A)"},{"roll":"6 - 8","loot":"Fine Mythical Beast Hide (300G/Red A)"},{"roll":"9+","loot":"Beautiful Mythical Beast Hide (800G/Gold Red A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Charm Bear","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"ycWYAmy7LtG4pagj","name":"Elder Manticore","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:elder-manticore","level":12,"monsterType":"Mythical Beast","intelligence":"High","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Neutral","soulscars":0,"languages":"Arcana, Sylvan","habitat":"Labyrinths","reputation":17,"weakness":22,"weakPoint":"Wind damage +3 points","initiative":20,"movementSpeed":"15 (4 Legs) / 23 (Flying)","fortitude":"14 (21)","willpower":"16 (23)","source":"BM","description":"This Mythical Beast is the superior species to the Lesser Manticore . Although its size and appearance have not changed, its power and knowledge have become awe-inspiring. They always know the location of the labyrinth where a powerful magic sword is hidden. However, they are still twisted and do not easily listen to Humanoids in normal circumstances. They usually ask for something unreasonable to do for their vast knowledge.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Claw (Front)","accuracy":"15 (22)","damage":"2d+14","evasion":"14 (21)","defense":10,"hp":{"value":124,"max":124},"mp":{"value":111,"max":111}},{"style":"Tail (Rear)","accuracy":"14 (21)","damage":"2d+17","evasion":"13 (20)","defense":8,"hp":{"value":110,"max":110},"mp":{"value":44,"max":44}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"Front","description":""},{"title":"► Truespeech Magic , Spiritualism Magic 12 Level / Magic Power 15 (22)","description":"If you have introduced Deep Magic , it can also cast Deep Magic at the same level and Magic Power."},{"title":"► Fairy Magic 9 Level / Magic Power 12 (19)","description":"Can cast Earth, Water/Ice, Fire, and Dark types. This does not change even if the contract pattern is adopted (see MA, p. 136)."},{"title":"◯ 🗨 Magic Aptitude","description":"They can use the Combat Feats [ Targeting ], [ Magic Convergence ], [ Magic Control ], and [ Metamagic/Targets ]."},{"title":"⏩ △ Techniques","description":"They may use the [ Cat's Eyes ], [ Beetleskin ], [ Gazelle Feet ], and [ Recovery (9 pts.) ] Techniques."},{"title":"Rear","description":""},{"title":"► Twin Strike &amp; Double Attack","description":"An Elder Manticore can make two Tail attacks each round, though each attack requires its own Accuracy check. They may choose to attack different characters with each attack."},{"title":"◯ Numbing Poison / 14 (21) / Fortitude / Negates","description":"If the Tail's attack hits and deals 1 or more points of applied damage, it will paralyze the target and reduce its Dexterity by -6 points (to a minimum of 0). This effect is cumulative, and when the Dexterity reaches 0, the target will be unable to make any melee or ranged attacks.\nIf the character has a fixed value, its Accuracy check is reduced by -1 for each effect of this poison, and the character cannot be attacked after three such effects.\nThis effect is Poison type and lasts for 1 hour."},{"title":"◯ Flight","description":"An Elder Manticore receives a +1 bonus to Accuracy and Evasion only for melee attacks.\nIf the Rear falls to 0 HP or lower, this unique skill cannot be used."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"2 - 6","loot":"Fine Mythical Beast Hide (300G/Red A)"},{"roll":"7 - 9","loot":"Beautiful Mythical Beast Hide (800G/Gold Red A)"},{"roll":"10+","loot":"Lustrous Mythical Beast Hide (4,400G/Gold Red S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Elder Manticore","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"zqpHNYXgW1j202je","name":"Cockatrice","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:cockatrice","level":10,"monsterType":"Mythical Beast","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Forests, Wilderness","reputation":15,"weakness":20,"weakPoint":"Water/Ice damage + 3 points","initiative":15,"movementSpeed":"18/18(Flying)","fortitude":"13 (20)","willpower":"13 (20)","source":"CR II p. 394","description":"Resembling a giant chicken with the legs and tail of a lizard, a Cockatrice is a dangerous beast, able to petrify anyone with its beak. Standing taller than most humanoids, Cockatrices are often hostile to anyone they perceive as threatening them or their nest. However, they absolutely hate Basilisks with every fiber of their being and will break off combat with others to attack one on sight.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Beak","accuracy":"13 (20)","damage":"2d+9","evasion":"11 (18)","defense":10,"hp":{"value":93,"max":93},"mp":{"value":27,"max":27}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Curse Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Continuous Attack II","description":"If a monster successfully hits a target in melee, it may make a second attack. It can make a third attack against the same target if a second attack hits."},{"title":"◯ Petrifying Beak / 11 (18) / Willpower / Negates","description":"If the Beak attack hits, the target becomes Petrified (Agility-12) (see ML p. 71).\nThis effect is the Curse type."},{"title":"⏩ △ Techniques","description":"They may use the [ Beetleskin ], [ Meditation ], and [ Recovery (5 points) ] Techniques."},{"title":"◯ Flight","description":"A Cockatrice receives a +1 bonus to Accuracy and Evasion only for melee attacks."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"2 - 6","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"7 - 12","loot":"Cockatrice Beak (1,000G/Red S)"},{"roll":"13+","loot":"Crimson Beak (3,200G/Red S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Cockatrice","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"ztpj8ix9f4mJN4LG","name":"Grinning Cat","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:grinning-cat","level":9,"monsterType":"Mythical Beast","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Neutral","soulscars":0,"languages":"Trade Common, Barbaric, Daemonic, Sylvan","habitat":"Shallows","reputation":16,"weakness":20,"weakPoint":"Water/Ice damage +3 points","initiative":16,"movementSpeed":"6 (4 Legs)","fortitude":"11(18)","willpower":"13(20)","source":"AB, p. 118","description":"Grinning Cat is a mythical beast, a large cat with purple fur who always wears a grinning smile showing its teeth. It possesses the supernatural ability to make itself invisible or appear at will, and loves using this power to tease others. However, its purpose is merely to enjoy watching others become confused and flustered, and it rarely attacks with clear malicious intent.\n\nPerhaps finding the environment of Shallow Abysses suitable, since the emergence of the Abyss, it has taken to wandering between Shallows in search of comfortable ones, settling in those it likes. Through this process, it has deepened its understanding of the Shallow and even acquired Abyssal Magic. Its claws are natural Abyssal Knives, and are traded at high prices among practitioners of Abyssal Magic.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Claws","accuracy":"12(19)","damage":"2d+9","evasion":"&#32;","defense":12,"hp":{"value":7,"max":7},"mp":{"value":32,"max":32}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"► Abyssal Magic 9 Level / Magic Power 11 (18)","description":"Extended effects can be used until the second round."},{"title":"◯🗨►Magic Aptitude","description":"They can use Combat Feats [ Targeting ], [ Magic Convergence ], [ Magic Control ], [ Hawk Eye ], [ Universal Metamagic ], and [ Wordbreak ]."},{"title":"►Dissolve into Space (Shallow)","description":"This effect can only be used within a Shallow Abyss.\nGrinning Cat disappears by melding into space. While in this disappeared state, it cannot be affected by any interference from others. While it can perceive its surroundings, it cannot directly interact with others. If the Shallow Grinning Cat was in collapses while it is in this state, it will be transported to either a random location in the world or another Shallow at random, where it will be forced to materialize."},{"title":"►Appear in Space (Shallow)","description":"This effect can only be used while being invisible through [►Dissolve into Space (Shallow)].\nGrinning Cat can appear at any location within its current Shallow Abyss that it has physically visited before.\nMany Grinning Cats are intimately familiar with their Shallow domain. In essence, they freely move about within the Shallow by teleporting at will."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Grinning Cat Claws (400G/Gold Red A)"},{"roll":"2 - 8","loot":"Beautiful Mythical Beast Hide (800G/Gold Red A)"},{"roll":"9+","loot":"Magnificent Mythical Beast Hide (2,100G/Gold Red S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Grinning Cat","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}